    "id": "c-algo-merge-sort",
    "subjectId": "Algorithms",
    "chapterId": "algo-sorting",
    "label": "Merge Sort & Inversion Counting",
    "name": "Merge Sort",
    "category": "Sorting Algorithms",
    "kind": "algorithm",
    "summary": "Divide-and-conquer comparison sorting algorithm. Divides array into two halves, recursively sorts them, and merges the sorted halves in linear time. Stable sort with guaranteed $O(n \\log n)$ in all cases.",
    "formula": "T(n) = 2T(n/2) + \\Theta(n) \\implies T(n) = \\Theta(n \\log n)",
    "keyFormulae": [
      "\\text{Max Comparisons in Merge phase: } n - 1",
      "\\text{Min Comparisons in Merge phase: } n / 2",
      "\\text{Total Comparisons in Merge Sort: } n \\log_2 n - n + 1",
      "\\text{Inversion count increment: } \\text{count} += (\\text{mid} - i + 1) \\text{ when } arr[i] > arr[j]"
    ],
    "complexity": "Time: Best/Avg/Worst $\\Theta(n \\log n)$, Space: $O(n)$ auxiliary array",
    "codeSnippet": "void merge(int arr[], int l, int m, int r) {\n    int n1 = m - l + 1, n2 = r - m;\n    int L[n1], R[n2];\n    for (int i = 0; i < n1; i++) L[i] = arr[l + i];\n    for (int j = 0; j < n2; j++) R[j] = arr[m + 1 + j];\n    int i = 0, j = 0, k = l;\n    while (i < n1 && j < n2) {\n        if (L[i] <= R[j]) arr[k++] = L[i++];\n        else arr[k++] = R[j++]; // Inversion occurs here\n    }\n    while (i < n1) arr[k++] = L[i++];\n    while (j < n2) arr[k++] = R[j++];\n}",
