    "summary": "Lossless data compression algorithm that assigns variable-length prefix-free binary codes to characters based on frequencies. Characters with higher frequency receive shorter codewords. Utilizes a Min-Heap.",
    "formula": "L = \\sum_{i=1}^n f_i \\cdot \\text{length}(c_i) \\implies \\text{Expected Bits per Char} = \\sum p_i \\cdot l_i",
    "keyFormulae": [
      "\\text{Total Internal Nodes in Tree with } n \\text{ leaves: } n - 1",
      "\\text{Total Nodes in Full Binary Huffman Tree: } 2n - 1",
      "\\text{Shannon Entropy Lower Bound: } H(X) = -\\sum p_i \\log_2 p_i \\le L < H(X) + 1"
    ],
    "complexity": "Time: $O(n \\log n)$ using a Min-Priority Queue. Space: $O(n)$ for tree nodes",
    "codeSnippet": "import heapq\ndef huffman_tree(freq_map):\n    heap = [[weight, [char, \"\"]] for char, weight in freq_map.items()]\n    heapq.heapify(heap)\n    while len(heap) > 1:\n        lo = heapq.heappop(heap)\n        hi = heapq.heappop(heap)\n        for pair in lo[1:]: pair[1] = '0' + pair[1]\n        for pair in hi[1:]: pair[1] = '1' + pair[1]\n        heapq.heappush(heap, [lo[0] + hi[0]] + lo[1:] + hi[1:])\n    return sorted(heapq.heappop(heap)[1:], key=lambda p: (len(p[-1]), p))",
    "imageUrl": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 460 140\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect width=\"460\" height=\"140\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#0F172A\"/><circle cx=\"230\" cy=\"25\" r=\"14\" fill=\"#38BDF8\"/><text x=\"230\" y=\"29\" font-size=\"9\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#0F172A\">100</text><line x1=\"218\" y1=\"35\" x2=\"150\" y2=\"65\" stroke=\"#94A3B8\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"175\" y=\"45\" fill=\"#38BDF8\" font-size=\"10\" font-family=\"monospace\">0</text><line x1=\"242\" y1=\"35\" x2=\"310\" y2=\"65\" stroke=\"#94A3B8\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"285\" y=\"45\" fill=\"#38BDF8\" font-size=\"10\" font-family=\"monospace\">1</text><circle cx=\"150\" cy=\"75\" r=\"13\" fill=\"#22C55E\"/><text x=\"150\" y=\"79\" font-size=\"9\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#0F172A\">A(45)</text><circle cx=\"310\" cy=\"75\" r=\"13\" fill=\"#F59E0B\"/><text x=\"310\" y=\"79\" font-size=\"9\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#0F172A\">55</text><text x=\"230\" y=\"120\" fill=\"#22C55E\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"monospace\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Prefix-Free Tree: A='0', B='10', C='11'</text></svg>",
    "commonTraps": [
      "Huffman codes are NOT uniquely determined (swapping 0/1 branch labels or tie-breaking order changes codewords), but the OPTIMAL TOTAL WEIGHT (bits) is UNIQUE.",
      "A full binary tree with $n$ leaves has exactly $n-1$ internal nodes and $2n-1$ total nodes."
    ],
