    "label": "Amortized Analysis (Aggregate, Accounting & Potential)",
    "name": "Amortized Analysis",
    "category": "String Matching",
    "kind": "technique",
    "summary": "Averages running time of an operation over a sequence of operations to guarantee average performance per operation in the worst-case sequence. Three methods: Aggregate Analysis, Accounting Method (credits/debits), and Potential Method (energy function $\\Phi$).",
    "formula": "\\hat{c}_i = c_i + \\Phi(D_i) - \\Phi(D_{i-1}) \\implies \\sum \\hat{c}_i = \\sum c_i + \\Phi(D_n) - \\Phi(D_0)",
    "keyFormulae": [
      "\\text{Aggregate Method: Total cost for } n \\text{ operations } T(n) \\implies \\text{Amortized Cost} = T(n)/n",
      "\\text{Accounting Method: Assign amortized charges } \\hat{c}_i \\ge c_i \\text{ so credit balance never drops below 0}",
      "\\text{Potential Method: } \\Phi(D_i) \\ge \\Phi(D_0) \\text{ ensures total amortized cost upper bounds total actual cost}",
      "\\text{Dynamic Array Doubling: } n \\text{ insertions take } O(n) \\text{ total time } \\implies O(1) \\text{ amortized}"
    ],
    "complexity": "Dynamic Array append: $O(1)$ amortized ($O(n)$ single worst-case expansion)",
    "codeSnippet": "# Dynamic Array Amortized Simulation\ndef dynamic_array_simulation(n):\n    capacity = 1; size = 0; total_copies = 0\n    for _ in range(n):\n        if size == capacity:\n            capacity *= 2\n            total_copies += size # Copying cost\n        size += 1\n        total_copies += 1 # Insert cost\n    return total_copies / n # Amortized cost <= 3",
    "imageUrl": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 460 130\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect width=\"460\" height=\"130\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#0F172A\"/><rect x=\"25\" y=\"20\" width=\"125\" height=\"85\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#1E293B\" stroke=\"#38BDF8\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"87\" y=\"45\" fill=\"#38BDF8\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">1. Aggregate</text><text x=\"87\" y=\"75\" fill=\"#CBD5E1\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Total T(n) / n</text><rect x=\"165\" y=\"20\" width=\"125\" height=\"85\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#1E293B\" stroke=\"#F59E0B\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"227\" y=\"45\" fill=\"#F59E0B\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2. Accounting</text><text x=\"227\" y=\"75\" fill=\"#CBD5E1\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Prepaid credits</text><rect x=\"305\" y=\"20\" width=\"130\" height=\"85\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#1E293B\" stroke=\"#22C55E\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"370\" y=\"45\" fill=\"#22C55E\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">3. Potential \u03a6</text><text x=\"370\" y=\"75\" fill=\"#CBD5E1\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">\u0394\u03a6 Energy stored</text></svg>",
    "commonTraps": [
      "Amortized cost is NOT Average Case analysis \u2014 it does NOT rely on probability or random inputs. It is a WORST-CASE guarantee over a sequence.",
      "The potential function $\\Phi$ must satisfy $\\Phi(D_n) \\ge \\Phi(D_0)$ for all $n$ to guarantee that total amortized cost is an upper bound."
    ],
