    "summary": "Deque allows insertion and deletion at both front and rear ends. Can be restricted to Input-Restricted (insert at one end, delete at both) or Output-Restricted. Priority Queue serves elements based on assigned priority using a Binary Heap.",
    "formula": "\\text{Priority Queue: Extract-Min/Max in } O(\\log n), \\; \\text{Insert in } O(\\log n), \\; \\text{Find-Min in } O(1)",
    "keyFormulae": [
      "\\text{Input-Restricted Deque: Insertion at ONE end, Deletion at BOTH ends}",
      "\\text{Output-Restricted Deque: Deletion at ONE end, Insertion at BOTH ends}",
      "\\text{Monotonic Deque: Maintains sorted window elements for sliding window max in } O(n)"
    ],
    "complexity": "Deque: $O(1)$ all operations, Priority Queue (Heap): $O(\\log n)$ insert/extract",
    "codeSnippet": "from collections import deque\n# Sliding Window Maximum using Monotonic Deque in O(n)\ndef max_sliding_window(nums, k):\n    q = deque()\n    res = []\n    for i, n in enumerate(nums):\n        while q and nums[q[-1]] < n: q.pop()\n        q.append(i)\n        if q[0] <= i - k: q.popleft() # Out of window\n        if i >= k - 1: res.append(nums[q[0]])\n    return res",
    "imageUrl": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 460 120\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect width=\"460\" height=\"120\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#0F172A\"/><rect x=\"80\" y=\"35\" width=\"300\" height=\"40\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#1E293B\" stroke=\"#38BDF8\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"40\" y=\"58\" fill=\"#22C55E\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">\u2190 Front \u2192</text><text x=\"230\" y=\"58\" fill=\"#CBD5E1\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"monospace\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Double-Ended Queue (Deque)</text><text x=\"420\" y=\"58\" fill=\"#22C55E\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">\u2190 Rear \u2192</text><text x=\"230\" y=\"100\" fill=\"#38BDF8\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"monospace\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Push/Pop from both ends in O(1)</text></svg>",
