    "kind": "algorithm",
    "summary": "Advanced tree structures for answering range queries (Range Sum, Range Minimum) and point updates in $O(\\log n)$ time. Segment tree uses a full binary tree array of size $4n$. Fenwick Tree (BIT) uses bitwise manipulation (`x & (-x)`) with $O(n)$ space.",
    "formula": "\\text{Fenwick Tree LSB isolate: } \\text{LSB}(x) = x \\;\\&\\; (-x)",
    "keyFormulae": [
      "\\text{Fenwick Tree Parent Update: } i = i + (i \\;\\&\\; -i)",
      "\\text{Fenwick Tree Prefix Sum Query: } i = i - (i \\;\\&\\; -i)",
      "\\text{Segment Tree Array Size: } 4n \\text{ elements}",
      "\\text{Query & Update Complexity: } O(\\log n)"
    ],
    "complexity": "Query: $O(\\log n)$, Point Update: $O(\\log n)$, Space: BIT $O(n)$, Segment Tree $O(4n)$",
    "codeSnippet": "# Binary Indexed Tree (Fenwick Tree) in Python\nclass FenwickTree:\n    def __init__(self, n):\n        self.tree = [0] * (n + 1)\n    def update(self, i, delta):\n        while i < len(self.tree):\n            self.tree[i] += delta\n            i += i & (-i) # Add LSB\n    def query(self, i):\n        s = 0\n        while i > 0:\n            s += self.tree[i]\n            i -= i & (-i) # Strip LSB\n        return s",
    "imageUrl": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 460 120\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect width=\"460\" height=\"120\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#0F172A\"/><rect x=\"25\" y=\"20\" width=\"190\" height=\"75\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#1E293B\" stroke=\"#38BDF8\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"45\" fill=\"#38BDF8\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Segment Tree (4n)</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"70\" fill=\"#CBD5E1\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Range Query: O(log n)</text><rect x=\"245\" y=\"20\" width=\"190\" height=\"75\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#1E293B\" stroke=\"#22C55E\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"340\" y=\"45\" fill=\"#22C55E\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Fenwick Tree BIT (n)</text><text x=\"340\" y=\"70\" fill=\"#CBD5E1\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Bitwise: i &amp; (-i)</text></svg>",
