    "id": "c-pds-cycle-detection",
    "subjectId": "Programming & Data Structures",
    "chapterId": "pds-graphs",
    "label": "Cycle Detection Algorithms in Graphs",
    "name": "Cycle Detection",
    "category": "Graphs & Advanced DS",
    "kind": "algorithm",
    "summary": "Methods for detecting cycles in directed and undirected graphs. In Directed Graphs, DFS tracks an active recursion stack (Back Edge). In Undirected Graphs, DFS checks for edges to visited non-parent nodes, or Disjoint Set Union (DSU) checks if both endpoints belong to the same connected component.",
    "formula": "\\text{Back Edge in DFS } \\iff \\text{Cycle in Directed/Undirected Graph}",
    "keyFormulae": [
      "\\text{Directed Graph: 3-Coloring DFS (White=Unvisited, Gray=Active in Stack, Black=Finished)}",
      "\\text{Undirected Graph via DSU: If } \\text{find}(u) == \\text{find}(v) \\implies \\text{Adding } (u,v) \\text{ forms a cycle}",
      "\\text{Acyclic Directed Graph } \\equiv \\text{DAG} \\iff \\text{Admits a valid Topological Sort}"
    ],
    "complexity": "Time: $O(V + E)$ using DFS / BFS, Space: $O(V)$",
    "codeSnippet": "# Cycle Detection in Undirected Graph using DSU\ndef has_cycle_undirected(V, edges):\n    parent = list(range(V))\n    def find(i):\n        if parent[i] == i: return i\n        parent[i] = find(parent[i])\n        return parent[i]\n    for u, v in edges:\n        ru, rv = find(u), find(v)\n        if ru == rv: return True # Cycle detected!\n        parent[ru] = rv\n    return False",
