    "summary": "Non-preemptive scheduling algorithm that allocates the CPU in order of arrival time using a FIFO queue. Simple and fair, but suffers from the Convoy Effect where short I/O-bound processes wait behind a long CPU-bound process, degrading average waiting time.",
    "formula": "\\text{Convoy Effect: 1 long CPU burst process dominates CPU } \\implies \\text{Average WT surges drastically}",
    "keyFormulae": [
      "\\text{Selection: } \\min(\\text{Arrival Time } AT)",
      "\\text{Non-preemptive: Running process retains CPU until voluntary burst completion or I/O block}",
      "\\text{Average WT is generally higher compared to shortest-first schemes}"
    ],
    "complexity": "Time: $O(n \\log n)$ to sort by arrival time, Gantt evaluation $O(n)$",
    "codeSnippet": "# FCFS Scheduling Simulation\ndef fcfs_schedule(processes):\n    # processes = [(pid, at, bt)]\n    processes.sort(key=lambda x: x[1]) # Sort by Arrival Time\n    curr_time = 0; schedule = []\n    for pid, at, bt in processes:\n        if curr_time < at: curr_time = at # CPU Idle\n        start = curr_time; curr_time += bt\n        schedule.append((pid, start, curr_time, curr_time - at, curr_time - at - bt))\n    return schedule",
