    "summary": "Scheduling across multiple CPU cores. Asymmetric Multiprocessing (AMP) designates one master core for OS scheduling. Symmetric Multiprocessing (SMP) lets all cores self-schedule from a global or per-core ready queue. CPU Affinity avoids cache invalidation overhead by keeping a process on the same core.",
    "formula": "\\text{Speedup (Amdahl's Law): } S(N) = \\frac{1}{(1 - P) + \\frac{P}{N}} \\quad (P = \\text{parallel fraction}, \\; N = \\text{cores})",
