    "id": "c-os-critical-section-problem",
    "subjectId": "Operating Systems",
    "chapterId": "os-synchronization",
    "label": "Critical Section Problem & 3 Core Criteria",
    "name": "Critical Section Problem",
    "category": "Process Synchronization & Deadlocks",
    "kind": "definition",
    "summary": "A Critical Section (CS) is a code segment accessing shared resources concurrently. A valid synchronization solution must strictly satisfy three requirements: Mutual Exclusion (mandatory), Progress (mandatory), and Bounded Waiting (starvation prevention).",
    "formula": "\\text{Valid Solution} = \\text{Mutual Exclusion (Mandatory)} \\land \\text{Progress (Mandatory)} \\land \\text{Bounded Waiting}",
    "keyFormulae": [
      "1. \\text{Mutual Exclusion: If process } P_i \\text{ is executing in CS, no other processes can execute in CS}",
      "2. \\text{Progress: If no process in CS, only processes NOT in remainder section participate in deciding who enters next; decision cannot be postponed indefinitely}",
      "3. \\text{Bounded Waiting: Limit on number of times other processes can enter CS after a process has requested entry (Prevents Starvation)}"
    ],
    "complexity": "Hardware lock check latency: Few clock cycles",
    "codeSnippet": "// Standard Critical Section Structure\ndo {\n    entry_section();   // Request entry\n    critical_section(); // Shared resource modification\n    exit_section();    // Release entry\n    remainder_section();// Non-critical work\n} while (true);",
    "imageUrl": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 460 130\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect width=\"460\" height=\"130\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#0F172A\"/><rect x=\"25\" y=\"20\" width=\"125\" height=\"85\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#1E293B\" stroke=\"#EF4444\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"87\" y=\"45\" fill=\"#EF4444\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">1. Mutual Exclusion</text><text x=\"87\" y=\"75\" fill=\"#CBD5E1\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">At most 1 process</text><text x=\"87\" y=\"92\" fill=\"#CBD5E1\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">in CS at a time</text><rect x=\"165\" y=\"20\" width=\"125\" height=\"85\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#1E293B\" stroke=\"#22C55E\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"227\" y=\"45\" fill=\"#22C55E\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2. Progress</text><text x=\"227\" y=\"75\" fill=\"#CBD5E1\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">No deadlock in</text><text x=\"227\" y=\"92\" fill=\"#CBD5E1\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">entry decision</text><rect x=\"305\" y=\"20\" width=\"130\" height=\"85\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#1E293B\" stroke=\"#38BDF8\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"370\" y=\"45\" fill=\"#38BDF8\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">3. Bounded Wait</text><text x=\"370\" y=\"75\" fill=\"#CBD5E1\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">No starvation for</text><text x=\"370\" y=\"92\" fill=\"#CBD5E1\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">waiting process</text></svg>",
    "commonTraps": [
      "Strict Alternation (`turn` variable alone) satisfies Mutual Exclusion and Bounded Waiting, but FAILS Progress because a process cannot enter CS twice if the other process is inactive.",
      "Processes in their REMAINDER section must NOT block other processes from entering CS (violates Progress)."
    ],
