    "id": "c-os-thrashing-working-set",
    "subjectId": "Operating Systems",
    "chapterId": "os-virtual-memory",
    "label": "Thrashing, Working-Set Model & Page Fault Frequency",
    "name": "Thrashing & Working-Set Model",
    "category": "Memory Management & Virtual Memory",
    "kind": "definition",
    "summary": "Thrashing occurs when a process spends more time paging (swapping pages in/out) than executing instructions, causing CPU utilization to collapse to near zero. Working-Set Model allocates frames based on locality window $\\Delta$; Page Fault Frequency (PFF) dynamically adjusts frame allocation.",
    "formula": "\\text{Thrashing Condition: } \\sum WSS_i > D \\quad (WSS = \\text{Working Set Size}, \\; D = \\text{Total Frames in RAM})",
    "keyFormulae": [
      "\\text{Working Set } W(t, \\Delta) = \\text{Set of distinct pages referenced in most recent } \\Delta \\text{ time units}",
      "\\text{Total Demand: } D = \\sum |WSS_i|; \\; \\text{If } D > \\text{Total Available Frames} \\implies \\text{Thrashing occurs}",
      "\\text{Page Fault Frequency (PFF): If fault rate } > \\text{Upper Threshold} \\to \\text{Allocate frame}; \\text{ If } < \\text{Lower} \\to \\text{Reclaim frame}"
    ],
    "complexity": "Locality of Reference: Temporal Locality (same page re-used) + Spatial Locality (adjacent pages)",
    "codeSnippet": "# Working Set Size Calculator in Python\ndef calculate_working_set(ref_stream, delta=4):\n    # ref_stream = [1, 2, 1, 3, 4, 1, 2]\n    working_sets = []\n    for i in range(len(ref_stream)):\n        window = ref_stream[max(0, i - delta + 1): i + 1]\n        working_sets.append(set(window))\n    return working_sets",
    "imageUrl": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 460 130\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect width=\"460\" height=\"130\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#0F172A\"/><path d=\"M50 100 Q150 20 230 30\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#22C55E\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><path d=\"M230 30 Q300 40 400 115\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#EF4444\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><line x1=\"230\" y1=\"10\" x2=\"230\" y2=\"115\" stroke=\"#F59E0B\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-dasharray=\"3\"/><text x=\"230\" y=\"20\" fill=\"#F59E0B\" font-size=\"10\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Thrashing Point</text><text x=\"320\" y=\"70\" fill=\"#EF4444\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"bold\">CPU Util Collapses</text></svg>",
    "commonTraps": [
      "When thrashing begins, OS short-term scheduler naively increases degree of multiprogramming, which accelerates the collapse.",
      "The ONLY cure for thrashing is to SUSPEND / SWAP OUT one or more entire processes to free physical frames."
    ],
