    "label": "OSI 7-Layer Reference Model",
    "kind": "definition",
    "summary": "The OSI (Open Systems Interconnection) model is a 7-layer conceptual framework (Physical, Data Link, Network, Transport, Session, Presentation, Application) that standardizes network communication functions. Each layer offers services to the layer above and uses services of the layer below through Service Access Points (SAPs).",
    "formula": "$\\text{Layers} = \\{1..7\\}$ \\quad $\\text{PDUs: Physical=bits, DLL=frames, Network=packets, Transport=segments}$",
    "prerequisites": [],
    "examRelevance": 5,
    "commonTraps": [
      "Presentation and Session layers are absent from the TCP/IP model; do not force a 1-to-1 mapping.",
      "Layer 5 (Session) is NOT responsible for routing or end-to-end connection - that is Layer 3/4."
    ],
    "pyqIds": [
      "GATE CSE 2001",
      "GATE CSE 2015 Set 2"
    ],
