    "chapterId": "cn-physical",
    "label": "Switching Techniques",
    "kind": "definition",
    "summary": "Switching routes data from source to destination. Circuit Switching establishes a dedicated path before data transfer. Packet Switching routes individual packets - either datagram (connectionless) or virtual circuit (connection-oriented). Message Switching is store-and-forward of complete messages.",
    "formula": "$T_{\\text{circuit}} = \\text{setup} + \\text{transfer} + \\text{teardown}$ \\quad $T_{\\text{packet}} = \\sum (T_t + T_p) \\text{ per hop}$",
    "prerequisites": [],
    "examRelevance": 5,
    "commonTraps": [
      "In packet switching, total delay is per-hop transmission + propagation + processing + queueing, summed across hops.",
      "Circuit switching reserves bandwidth even when idle; packet switching uses bandwidth on demand."
    ],
