    "label": "Go-Back-N ARQ",
    "kind": "algorithm",
    "summary": "Sender can have up to N unacknowledged frames (window size N). On error, sender retransmits all frames from the lost one onwards. Receiver window size is 1 - only accepts in-order frames. Sequence numbers needed: at least N+1 to avoid ambiguity, hence window size W <= 2^n - 1 where n is sequence bits.",
    "formula": "W \\leq 2^n - 1",
    "prerequisites": [],
    "examRelevance": 5,
    "commonTraps": [
      "GBN requires W <= 2^n - 1 (NOT 2^n), otherwise the sender cannot distinguish an ACK for old frame vs. new frame.",
      "Receiver window for GBN is always 1, regardless of sender's window size."
    ],
