    "id": "c-dm-propositional-logic",
    "subjectId": "Discrete Mathematics",
    "chapterId": "dm-logic",
    "label": "Propositional Logic Connectives, Truth Tables & WFF",
    "name": "Propositional Logic Basics",
    "category": "Propositional & First-Order Predicate Logic",
    "kind": "definition",
    "summary": "Mathematical study of declarative statements that are either TRUE ($T / 1$) or FALSE ($F / 0$), but not both. Core Connectives: Negation ($\\neg P$), Conjunction ($P \\land Q$), Disjunction ($P \\lor Q$), Conditional / Implication ($P \\to Q$: False ONLY when $P=T, Q=F$), Biconditional ($P \\leftrightarrow Q$: True when both share same truth value), Exclusive OR ($P \\oplus Q$). Precedence: $\\neg > \\land > \\lor > \\to > \\leftrightarrow$.",
    "formula": "P \\to Q \\equiv \\neg P \\lor Q \\quad | \\quad P \\leftrightarrow Q \\equiv (P \\to Q) \\land (Q \\to P) \\equiv (P \\land Q) \\lor (\\neg P \\land \\neg Q)",
    "keyFormulae": [
      "\\text{Conditional Truth Table: } T \\to T = T, \\; T \\to F = F, \\; F \\to T = T, \\; F \\to F = T \\; (\\text{Vacuously True when } P=F!)",
      "\\text{Biconditional: } P \\leftrightarrow Q \\equiv (P \\land Q) \\lor (\\neg P \\land \\neg Q) \\equiv \\neg(P \\oplus Q)",
      "\\text{Exclusive OR (XOR): } P \\oplus Q \\equiv (P \\land \\neg Q) \\lor (\\neg P \\land Q)",
      "\\text{Well-Formed Formulas (WFF): Syntactically valid propositional logic expressions}"
    ],
    "complexity": "Truth Table Evaluation: $2^n$ rows for $n$ propositional variables",
    "codeSnippet": "# Truth Table Generator in Python\ndef truth_table_implication():\n    print(\"P\\tQ\\tP -> Q\\tP <-> Q\\tP (+) Q\")\n    for P in [True, False]:\n        for Q in [True, False]:\n            imp = (not P) or Q\n            bicond = P == Q\n            xor = P != Q\n            print(f\"{P}\\t{Q}\\t{imp}\\t{bicond}\\t{xor}\")",
    "imageUrl": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 460 120\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect width=\"460\" height=\"120\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#0F172A\"/><rect x=\"25\" y=\"20\" width=\"190\" height=\"75\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#1E293B\" stroke=\"#38BDF8\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"45\" fill=\"#38BDF8\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">P \u2192 Q (Implication)</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"70\" fill=\"#CBD5E1\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">False ONLY when T \u2192 F</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"88\" fill=\"#22C55E\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">\u2261 \u00acP \u2228 Q</text><rect x=\"245\" y=\"20\" width=\"190\" height=\"75\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#1E293B\" stroke=\"#22C55E\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"340\" y=\"45\" fill=\"#22C55E\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">P \u2194 Q (Biconditional)</text><text x=\"340\" y=\"70\" fill=\"#CBD5E1\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">True when P == Q</text><text x=\"340\" y=\"88\" fill=\"#22C55E\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">\u2261 (P \u2192 Q) \u2227 (Q \u2192 P)</text></svg>",
    "commonTraps": [
      "$P \\to Q$ is FALSE ONLY when $P$ is True and $Q$ is False. If $P$ is False, $P \\to Q$ is VACUOUSLY TRUE regardless of $Q$!",
      "Connective precedence: $\\neg$ has highest precedence, followed by $\\land$, then $\\lor$, then $\\to$, then $\\leftrightarrow$."
    ],
