    "label": "Special Graph Families: $K_n, C_n, W_n, Q_n$ & Regular Graphs",
    "name": "Special Graph Families",
    "category": "Graph Theory",
    "kind": "definition",
    "summary": "Archetypal graph architectures in GATE: 1. Complete Graph $K_n$: Every pair adjacent ($|E| = \\binom{n}{2}, \\deg = n-1$); 2. Cycle $C_n$ ($n \\ge 3$): 2-regular simple cycle ($|V|=n, |E|=n$); 3. Wheel Graph $W_n$ ($n \\ge 3$): $C_n$ connected to central hub vertex ($|V|=n+1, |E|=2n$); 4. Hypercube / $n$-Cube $Q_n$: Vertices represented by $n$-bit strings, edges between strings differing in 1 bit ($|V|=2^n, |E|=n 2^{n-1}$, $n$-regular, Bipartite); 5. $k$-Regular Graph: Every vertex has degree $k$ ($2|E| = n k$).",
    "formula": "K_n: E = \\binom{n}{2}, \\quad W_n: (V=n+1, E=2n), \\quad Q_n: (V=2^n, E=n 2^{n-1}) \\quad | \\quad \\text{Regular: } 2E = n k",
