    "id": "c-dm-eulerian-graphs",
    "subjectId": "Discrete Mathematics",
    "chapterId": "dm-graphs",
    "label": "Eulerian Graphs, Circuits & Trails (Fleury's Theorem)",
    "name": "Eulerian Graphs & Circuits",
    "category": "Graph Theory",
    "kind": "theorem",
    "summary": "Eulerian Trail: A walk traversing EVERY EDGE in $G$ exactly once. Eulerian Circuit: A closed walk traversing every edge exactly once and returning to start. Euler's Theorems: 1. Undirected Connected Graph is Eulerian (has Eulerian Circuit) IF AND ONLY IF EVERY vertex has EVEN degree; 2. Undirected Connected Graph has an Eulerian Trail IF AND ONLY IF EXACTLY 0 or 2 vertices have ODD degree (Trail starts at one odd-degree vertex and ends at the other); 3. Directed Graph is Eulerian IF AND ONLY IF it is strongly connected and $\\text{in-deg}(v) = \\text{out-deg}(v)$ for all $v$.",
    "formula": "\\text{Eulerian Circuit} \\iff \\forall v, \\deg(v) \\text{ is EVEN} \\quad | \\quad \\text{Eulerian Trail} \\iff \\text{Exactly 0 or 2 vertices have ODD degree}",
    "keyFormulae": [
      "\\text{Eulerian Circuit (Undirected): Connected } + \\text{ ALL vertices have EVEN degree}",
      "\\text{Eulerian Trail (Undirected): Connected } + \\text{ EXACTLY 2 vertices have ODD degree (Starts at one, ends at other)}",
      "\\text{Directed Eulerian Circuit: Strongly Connected } + \\text{in-degree}(v) = \\text{out-degree}(v) \\; \\forall v",
      "\\text{Complete Graph } K_n \\text{ is Eulerian } \\iff n \\text{ is ODD} \\; (\\deg(v) = n-1 \\text{ is even})",
      "\\text{Complete Bipartite } K_{m, n} \\text{ is Eulerian } \\iff m \\text{ is EVEN and } n \\text{ is EVEN}"
    ],
    "complexity": "Eulerian Path Finding: $O(V + E)$ linear time via Hierholzer's Algorithm",
    "codeSnippet": "# Eulerian Graph Diagnostic in Python\ndef check_eulerian(graph):\n    # graph: {u: [neighbors]}\n    odd_deg_nodes = [u for u in graph if len(graph[u]) % 2 != 0]\n    if len(odd_deg_nodes) == 0:\n        return 'Eulerian Circuit (Every vertex even degree)'\n    elif len(odd_deg_nodes) == 2:\n        return f'Eulerian Trail between {odd_deg_nodes[0]} and {odd_deg_nodes[1]}'\n    else:\n        return 'Non-Eulerian (Cannot traverse all edges once)'",
    "imageUrl": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 460 120\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect width=\"460\" height=\"120\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#0F172A\"/><rect x=\"25\" y=\"20\" width=\"190\" height=\"75\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#1E293B\" stroke=\"#22C55E\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"45\" fill=\"#22C55E\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Eulerian Circuit</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"70\" fill=\"#CBD5E1\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Connected + ALL vertices EVEN deg</text><rect x=\"245\" y=\"20\" width=\"190\" height=\"75\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#1E293B\" stroke=\"#38BDF8\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"340\" y=\"45\" fill=\"#38BDF8\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Eulerian Trail</text><text x=\"340\" y=\"70\" fill=\"#CBD5E1\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Connected + EXACTLY 2 ODD deg</text></svg>",
    "commonTraps": [
      "$K_n$ is Eulerian IF AND ONLY IF $n$ is ODD (because $\\deg = n-1$ must be even).",
      "$K_{m,n}$ is Eulerian IF AND ONLY IF BOTH $m$ and $n$ are EVEN.",
      "An Eulerian graph requires traversing all EDGES once; a Hamiltonian graph requires visiting all VERTICES once."
    ],
