    "id": "c-em-vector-spaces",
    "subjectId": "Engineering Mathematics",
    "chapterId": "em-linear-algebra",
    "label": "Vector Spaces, Subspaces & Fundamental Subspaces",
    "name": "Vector Spaces & Subspaces",
    "category": "Linear Algebra",
    "kind": "definition",
    "summary": "A Vector Space $V$ over field $\\mathbb{F}$ is a set closed under vector addition and scalar multiplication satisfying 8 axioms. Subspace Test: $W \\subseteq V$ is a subspace IF AND ONLY IF: 1. $0 \\in W$; 2. $u, v \\in W \\implies u + v \\in W$; 3. $c \\in \\mathbb{F}, u \\in W \\implies c u \\in W$. Four Fundamental Subspaces of matrix $A_{m \\times n}$: 1. Column Space $\\text{Col}(A) \\subseteq \\mathbb{R}^m$ (dim $r$); 2. Row Space $\\text{Row}(A) \\subseteq \\mathbb{R}^n$ (dim $r$); 3. Null Space $\\text{Null}(A) \\subseteq \\mathbb{R}^n$ (dim $n-r$); 4. Left Null Space $\\text{Null}(A^T) \\subseteq \\mathbb{R}^m$ (dim $m-r$).",
    "formula": "W \\le V \\iff 0 \\in W \\land \\forall u, v \\in W, \\; c \\in \\mathbb{F} \\implies (u + cv \\in W)",
    "keyFormulae": [
      "\\text{Subspace Criterion: } 0 \\in W, \\quad u + v \\in W, \\quad c u \\in W",
      "\\text{Line Through Origin in } \\mathbb{R}^2 \\text{ is a subspace; Line not passing through origin is NOT}",
      "\\text{Four Fundamental Subspaces:}",
      "\\dim(\\text{Col}(A)) = \\dim(\\text{Row}(A)) = r, \\quad \\dim(\\text{Null}(A)) = n - r, \\quad \\dim(\\text{Null}(A^T)) = m - r",
      "\\text{Orthogonal Complements: } \\text{Row}(A) \\perp \\text{Null}(A) \\text{ in } \\mathbb{R}^n, \\quad \\text{Col}(A) \\perp \\text{Null}(A^T) \\text{ in } \\mathbb{R}^m"
    ],
    "complexity": "Subspace Test: $O(1)$ algebraic linearity check",
    "codeSnippet": "-- Subspace Identification Rules:\n-- Set W                                Is Subspace?  Reason\n-- {(x, y) | 2x - 3y = 0}               YES           Plane through origin (contains (0,0))\n-- {(x, y) | 2x - 3y = 5}               NO            Does not contain origin (0,0)\n-- {(x, y) | x >= 0, y >= 0}            NO            Not closed under negative scalar multiplication\n-- {Matrices A | Tr(A) = 0}             YES           Linear trace condition",
    "imageUrl": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 460 120\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect width=\"460\" height=\"120\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#0F172A\"/><rect x=\"25\" y=\"20\" width=\"190\" height=\"75\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#1E293B\" stroke=\"#38BDF8\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"45\" fill=\"#38BDF8\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Subspace Invariant</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"70\" fill=\"#22C55E\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Must contain Origin (0,0)</text><rect x=\"245\" y=\"20\" width=\"190\" height=\"75\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#1E293B\" stroke=\"#22C55E\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"340\" y=\"45\" fill=\"#22C55E\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Orthogonal Subspaces</text><text x=\"340\" y=\"70\" fill=\"#22C55E\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Row(A) \u27c2 Null(A) in R^n</text></svg>",
    "commonTraps": [
      "Any set that does not contain the ZERO vector ($0$) CANNOT be a vector subspace.",
      "The union of two subspaces is a subspace IF AND ONLY IF one is contained in the other."
    ],
