    "id": "c-em-continuity-differentiability",
    "subjectId": "Engineering Mathematics",
    "chapterId": "em-calculus",
    "label": "Continuity, Differentiability & Types of Discontinuities",
    "name": "Continuity & Differentiability",
    "category": "Calculus",
    "kind": "definition",
    "summary": "1. Continuity: $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=a$ IF AND ONLY IF Left Hand Limit $=$ Right Hand Limit $=$ Function Value: $\\lim_{x \\to a^-} f(x) = \\lim_{x \\to a^+} f(x) = f(a)$; 2. Differentiability: $f(x)$ is differentiable at $x=a$ if $f'(a) = \\lim_{h \\to 0} \\frac{f(a+h)-f(a)}{h}$ exists ($LHD = RHD$); 3. Differentiability $\\implies$ Continuity (The converse is FALSE, e.g. $f(x)=|x|$ is continuous at $x=0$ but not differentiable due to sharp cusp); 4. Discontinuity Types: Removable (limit exists $\\ne f(a)$), Jump ($LHL \\ne RHL$), Essential / Infinite.",
    "formula": "f \\text{ Differentiable} \\implies f \\text{ Continuous} \\quad (\\text{Converse is False: } f(x)=|x| \\text{ at } x=0)",
    "keyFormulae": [
      "\\text{Continuity Test: } \\lim_{x \\to a^-} f(x) = \\lim_{x \\to a^+} f(x) = f(a)",
      "\\text{Differentiability Test: } LHD = \\lim_{h \\to 0^-} \\frac{f(a+h)-f(a)}{h} = RHD = \\lim_{h \\to 0^+} \\frac{f(a+h)-f(a)}{h}",
      "\\text{Sharp Corners / Cusps: } f(x) = |x-c| \\implies \\text{Continuous everywhere, but NOT differentiable at } x=c",
      "\\text{Removable Discontinuity: } \\lim_{x \\to a} f(x) \\text{ exists, but } \\lim_{x \\to a} f(x) \\ne f(a)"
    ],
    "complexity": "Diagnostic: $O(1)$ evaluation of left/right limits and derivatives",
    "codeSnippet": "-- Classical Continuity & Differentiability Examples:\n-- Function f(x)    At x=0 Continuous?    At x=0 Differentiable?\n-- |x|              YES (LHL=RHL=0)       NO (LHD = -1, RHD = +1)\n-- x * sin(1/x)     YES (0 by Squeeze)    NO (lim cos(1/x) oscillates)\n-- x^2 * sin(1/x)   YES                   YES (f'(0) = 0 by Squeeze!)",
    "imageUrl": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 460 120\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect width=\"460\" height=\"120\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#0F172A\"/><rect x=\"25\" y=\"20\" width=\"190\" height=\"75\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#1E293B\" stroke=\"#38BDF8\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"45\" fill=\"#38BDF8\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Continuity Condition</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"70\" fill=\"#22C55E\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">LHL = RHL = f(a)</text><rect x=\"245\" y=\"20\" width=\"190\" height=\"75\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#1E293B\" stroke=\"#22C55E\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"340\" y=\"45\" fill=\"#22C55E\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Differentiable \u27f9 Cont</text><text x=\"340\" y=\"70\" fill=\"#CBD5E1\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">|x| is cont, but not diff at 0</text></svg>",
    "commonTraps": [
      "Continuity does NOT imply differentiability ($f(x)=|x|$ has sharp corner at origin, $LHD=-1 \\ne RHD=+1$).",
      "$x \\sin(1/x)$ is continuous at $x=0$ (set $f(0)=0$) but NOT differentiable; $x^2 \\sin(1/x)$ IS differentiable at $x=0$."
    ],
