    "id": "c-em-probability-axioms",
    "subjectId": "Engineering Mathematics",
    "chapterId": "em-probability",
    "label": "Axiomatic Probability, Mutually Exclusive & Independent Events",
    "name": "Probability Axioms & Independence",
    "category": "Probability & Statistics",
    "kind": "definition",
    "summary": "Kolmogorov's Probability Axioms on Sample Space $S$: 1. Non-negativity: $P(A) \\ge 0$; 2. Normalization: $P(S) = 1$; 3. Additivity: For mutually exclusive events ($A \\cap B = \\emptyset$), $P(A \\cup B) = P(A) + P(B)$. General Addition Rule: $P(A \\cup B) = P(A) + P(B) - P(A \\cap B)$. Independent Events: $A$ and $B$ are independent IF AND ONLY IF $P(A \\cap B) = P(A) P(B)$. (If $P(A), P(B) > 0$, independent events can NEVER be mutually exclusive!).",
    "formula": "P(A \\cup B) = P(A) + P(B) - P(A \\cap B) \\quad | \\quad A, B \\text{ Independent} \\iff P(A \\cap B) = P(A) P(B)",
    "keyFormulae": [
      "\\text{Complement Rule: } P(A') = 1 - P(A)",
      "\\text{Mutually Exclusive Events: } A \\cap B = \\emptyset \\implies P(A \\cap B) = 0 \\implies P(A \\cup B) = P(A) + P(B)",
      "\\text{Independent Events: } P(A \\cap B) = P(A) P(B) \\implies P(A \\mid B) = P(A)",
      "\\text{Mutual Exclusivity vs Independence: Mutually exclusive events with non-zero probability are ALWAYS DEPENDENT!}",
      "\\text{Pairwise vs Mutual Independence: 3 events can be pairwise independent without being mutually independent}"
    ],
    "complexity": "Probability Bounds: $0 \\le P(A) \\le 1$ with $O(1)$ set arithmetic",
    "codeSnippet": "-- Probability Rules Diagnostic:\n-- Mutually Exclusive: P(A \u2229 B) = 0   (Events CANNOT happen together)\n-- Independent:        P(A \u2229 B) = P(A) * P(B) (Occurrence of B does NOT affect A)\n-- If P(A) = 0.4 and P(B) = 0.5 are Independent:\n-- P(A \u222a B) = 0.4 + 0.5 - (0.4 * 0.5) = 0.9 - 0.2 = 0.7!",
    "imageUrl": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 460 120\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect width=\"460\" height=\"120\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#0F172A\"/><rect x=\"25\" y=\"20\" width=\"190\" height=\"75\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#1E293B\" stroke=\"#38BDF8\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"45\" fill=\"#38BDF8\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Addition Rule</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"70\" fill=\"#CBD5E1\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">P(A\u222aB) = P(A)+P(B)-P(A\u2229B)</text><rect x=\"245\" y=\"20\" width=\"190\" height=\"75\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#1E293B\" stroke=\"#22C55E\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"340\" y=\"45\" fill=\"#22C55E\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Independent Events</text><text x=\"340\" y=\"70\" fill=\"#22C55E\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">P(A \u2229 B) = P(A) \u00b7 P(B)</text></svg>",
    "commonTraps": [
      "DO NOT confuse Mutually Exclusive ($P(A \\cap B) = 0$) with Independent ($P(A \\cap B) = P(A) P(B)$) \u2014 they are completely different concepts!",
      "If two events with non-zero probability are mutually exclusive, knowing that one occurred means the other CANNOT occur $\\implies$ they are strongly DEPENDENT."
    ],
