    "id": "c-em-random-variables-continuous",
    "subjectId": "Engineering Mathematics",
    "chapterId": "em-probability",
    "label": "Continuous Random Variables: PDF, CDF, Expectation & Variance",
    "name": "Continuous Random Variables",
    "category": "Probability & Statistics",
    "kind": "definition",
    "summary": "Random variable taking uncountably infinite values in intervals: 1. Probability Density Function (PDF) $f(x)$: Satisfies $f(x) \\ge 0$ and $\\int_{-\\infty}^\\infty f(x) dx = 1$; 2. Interval Probability: $P(a \\le X \\le b) = \\int_a^b f(x) dx$; 3. Single Point Probability is ALWAYS ZERO: $P(X = c) = 0$; 4. Cumulative Distribution Function (CDF): $F(x) = P(X \\le x) = \\int_{-\\infty}^x f(t) dt \\implies f(x) = \\frac{d}{dx} F(x)$; 5. Expectation: $E[X] = \\int_{-\\infty}^\\infty x f(x) dx$; 6. Variance: $\\text{Var}(X) = \\int_{-\\infty}^\\infty x^2 f(x) dx - (E[X])^2$.",
    "formula": "\\int_{-\\infty}^\\infty f(x) dx = 1 \\quad | \\quad P(a \\le X \\le b) = \\int_a^b f(x) dx \\quad | \\quad f(x) = \\frac{d}{dx} F(x) \\quad | \\quad P(X = c) = 0",
    "keyFormulae": [
      "\\text{PDF Normalization: } \\int_{-\\infty}^\\infty f(x) dx = 1",
      "\\text{Relation between PDF and CDF: } f(x) = F'(x) = \\frac{d}{dx} F(x)",
      "\\text{Single Point Probability: } P(X = c) = 0 \\implies P(a \\le X \\le b) = P(a < X < b)",
      "\\text{Expectation (Mean): } E[X] = \\int_{-\\infty}^\\infty x f(x) dx",
      "\\text{Variance: } \\text{Var}(X) = \\int_{-\\infty}^\\infty (x - \\mu)^2 f(x) dx = E[X^2] - (E[X])^2"
    ],
    "complexity": "Evaluation: $O(1)$ symbolic calculus integration",
    "codeSnippet": "# Continuous PDF Verification in Python\nimport sympy as sp\nx = sp.Symbol('x')\nk = sp.Symbol('k')\n# PDF f(x) = k * x for 0 <= x <= 2\n# Find k: \u222b_0^2 k*x dx = 1 -> k * [x^2 / 2]_0^2 = 2k = 1 -> k = 0.5\nf = 0.5 * x\nE_X = sp.integrate(x * f, (x, 0, 2)) # \u222b_0^2 0.5 x^2 dx = 0.5 * (8/3) = 4/3\nE_X2 = sp.integrate((x ** 2) * f, (x, 0, 2)) # \u222b_0^2 0.5 x^3 dx = 0.5 * 4 = 2\nVar_X = E_X2 - (E_X ** 2) # 2 - 16/9 = 2/9\nprint(f'E[X] = {E_X}, Var(X) = {Var_X}')",
    "imageUrl": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 460 120\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect width=\"460\" height=\"120\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#0F172A\"/><rect x=\"25\" y=\"20\" width=\"190\" height=\"75\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#1E293B\" stroke=\"#38BDF8\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"45\" fill=\"#38BDF8\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">PDF Normalization</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"70\" fill=\"#22C55E\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">\u222b_-\u221e^\u221e f(x) dx = 1</text><rect x=\"245\" y=\"20\" width=\"190\" height=\"75\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#1E293B\" stroke=\"#22C55E\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"340\" y=\"45\" fill=\"#22C55E\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Point Probability</text><text x=\"340\" y=\"70\" fill=\"#22C55E\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">P(X = c) = 0 for continuous</text></svg>",
    "commonTraps": [
      "For ANY continuous random variable, $P(X = c) = 0$ for any exact single point $c$. Thus, $P(a \\le X \\le b) = P(a < X < b)$.",
      "$f(x)$ is a probability DENSITY, not a probability \u2014 $f(x)$ CAN exceed 1 (as long as total integral is 1)."
    ],
