    "id": "c-ga-critical-reasoning",
    "subjectId": "General Aptitude",
    "chapterId": "ga-verbal",
    "label": "Critical Reasoning: Assumptions, Strengthening & Weakening Arguments",
    "name": "Critical Reasoning",
    "category": "Verbal Aptitude",
    "kind": "technique",
    "summary": "Analyzing logical structure of arguments: $\\text{Premise} + \\text{Unstated Assumption} \\implies \\text{Conclusion}$. Question Types: 1. Identify Assumption: The unstated premise necessary for conclusion to hold (Negation Test: If negating the assumption collapses the argument, it is the correct assumption!); 2. Strengthen Argument: Introduces new evidence supporting causal link; 3. Weaken Argument: Introduces alternative cause, counterexample, or breaks link between premise and conclusion.",
    "formula": "\\text{Argument} = \\text{Premise} + \\text{Assumption} \\implies \\text{Conclusion} \\quad | \\quad \\text{Negation Test for Assumption}",
    "keyFormulae": [
      "\\text{Assumption Negation Test: Negate choice } \\implies \\text{If conclusion fails, choice is MANDATORY assumption}",
      "\\text{Weaken Argument: Find alternative explanation (} C \\implies B \\text{ instead of } A \\implies B)",
      "\\text{Strengthen Argument: Eliminate alternative explanations or validate data accuracy}"
    ],
    "complexity": "Evaluation: 2-step formal assumption negation",
    "codeSnippet": "-- Assumption Negation Test Example:\n-- Argument: 'Sales of electric cars rose 50%. Therefore, carbon emissions dropped.'\n-- Candidate Assumption: 'The electricity used to charge these cars was not generated by high-emission coal.'\n-- Negation: 'The electricity WAS generated by high-emission coal.'\n-- Effect: Negation completely DESTROYS the conclusion -> Assumption is valid!",
    "imageUrl": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 460 120\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect width=\"460\" height=\"120\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#0F172A\"/><rect x=\"25\" y=\"20\" width=\"190\" height=\"75\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#1E293B\" stroke=\"#38BDF8\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"45\" fill=\"#38BDF8\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Premise + Assumption</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"70\" fill=\"#CBD5E1\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">\u27f9 Conclusion</text><rect x=\"245\" y=\"20\" width=\"190\" height=\"75\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#1E293B\" stroke=\"#22C55E\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"340\" y=\"45\" fill=\"#22C55E\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Negation Test</text><text x=\"340\" y=\"70\" fill=\"#22C55E\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Negating assumption destroys conclusion</text></svg>",
    "commonTraps": [
      "An assumption must be UNSTATED (if it is explicitly written in the text, it is a premise, NOT an assumption!).",
      "Correlation does NOT imply causation (assuming $A$ caused $B$ merely because $A$ preceded $B$ is the classic flawed assumption)."
    ],
