    "id": "c-ga-percentage-profit",
    "subjectId": "General Aptitude",
    "chapterId": "ga-quantitative",
    "label": "Percentages, Successive Changes, Profit, Loss & Discount",
    "name": "Percentages, Profit & Loss",
    "category": "Quantitative Aptitude",
    "kind": "technique",
    "summary": "1. Successive Percentage Changes: Net change of $+a\\%$ followed by $+b\\%$ is $\\text{Net}\\% = a + b + \\frac{ab}{100}\\%$; 2. Percentage AB Rule: If $A$ is $x\\%$ more than $B$, then $B$ is $\\frac{x}{100+x} \\times 100\\%$ less than $A$; 3. Profit & Loss: $\\text{Profit}\\% = \\frac{SP - CP}{CP} \\times 100$, $\\text{Loss}\\% = \\frac{CP - SP}{CP} \\times 100$ (Always calculated on Cost Price $CP$!); 4. Marked Price ($MP$) & Discount ($D\\%$): $SP = MP \\times \\left(1 - \\frac{D}{100}\\right)$, $\\frac{MP}{CP} = \\frac{100 + \\text{Profit}\\%}{100 - \\text{Discount}\\%}$; 5. False Weights: $\\text{Gain}\\% = \\frac{\\text{Error}}{\\text{True Value} - \\text{Error}} \\times 100\\%$.",
    "formula": "\\text{Net}\\% = a + b + \\frac{ab}{100} \\quad | \\quad \\frac{MP}{CP} = \\frac{100 + P\\%}{100 - D\\%} \\quad | \\quad \\text{False Weight Gain} = \\frac{\\text{Error}}{\\text{True} - \\text{Error}} \\times 100\\%",
    "keyFormulae": [
      "\\text{Successive Percentages: } \\text{Net} = a + b + \\frac{ab}{100} \\; (\\text{Use negative signs for discounts/losses})",
      "\\text{Expenditure Constant: If price rises by } r\\%, \\text{ consumption must drop by } \\frac{r}{100+r} \\times 100\\%",
      "\\text{Marked Price vs Cost Price Ratio: } \\frac{MP}{CP} = \\frac{100 + \\text{Profit}\\%}{100 - \\text{Discount}\\%}",
      "\\text{Two items sold at same SP, one at } +x\\% \\text{ profit and other at } -x\\% \\text{ loss: Always Net Loss } = \\frac{x^2}{100}\\%"
    ],
    "complexity": "Evaluation: Instant $O(1)$ percentage formula lookup",
    "codeSnippet": "-- Successive Discount Example (30% + 20% discount):\n-- a = -30, b = -20\n-- Net Discount = -30 + (-20) + [(-30)*(-20)]/100 = -50 + 6 = -44% (Equivalent to single 44% discount!)\n-- Equal SP Loss Rule:\n-- Two laptops sold for Rs 40,000 each; 1st at +20% gain, 2nd at -20% loss.\n-- Net result is ALWAYS LOSS = (20^2)/100 = 4% Loss!",
    "imageUrl": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 460 120\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect width=\"460\" height=\"120\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#0F172A\"/><rect x=\"25\" y=\"20\" width=\"190\" height=\"75\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#1E293B\" stroke=\"#38BDF8\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"45\" fill=\"#38BDF8\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Successive Changes</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"70\" fill=\"#22C55E\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">a + b + (ab / 100)%</text><rect x=\"245\" y=\"20\" width=\"190\" height=\"75\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#1E293B\" stroke=\"#22C55E\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"340\" y=\"45\" fill=\"#22C55E\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Equal SP Loss Rule</text><text x=\"340\" y=\"70\" fill=\"#EF4444\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Net Loss = (x^2 / 100)%</text></svg>",
    "commonTraps": [
      "When two items are sold at the same SP with equal gain/loss $x\\%$, the overall transaction is ALWAYS a NET LOSS of $\\frac{x^2}{100}\\%$ (NOT 0%!).",
      "Profit percentage is ALWAYS calculated on Cost Price ($CP$), NOT Selling Price ($SP$) unless explicitly specified."
    ],
