    "summary": "1. 2-Set Principle of Inclusion-Exclusion: $n(A \\cup B) = n(A) + n(B) - n(A \\cap B)$; 2. 3-Set Principle of Inclusion-Exclusion: $n(A \\cup B \\cup C) = n(A) + n(B) + n(C) - [n(A \\cap B) + n(B \\cap C) + n(C \\cap A)] + n(A \\cap B \\cap C)$; 3. Exactly One Set: $\\sum n(A) - 2 \\sum n(A \\cap B) + 3 n(A \\cap B \\cap C)$; 4. Exactly Two Sets: $\\sum n(A \\cap B) - 3 n(A \\cap B \\cap C)$; 5. Graphical Categorization: Representing real-world relationships with overlapping geometric circles.",
    "formula": "n(A \\cup B \\cup C) = \\sum n(A) - \\sum n(A \\cap B) + n(A \\cap B \\cap C)",
    "keyFormulae": [
      "\\text{2-Set Union: } n(A \\cup B) = n(A) + n(B) - n(A \\cap B)",
      "\\text{3-Set Union: } n(A \\cup B \\cup C) = n(A)+n(B)+n(C) - [n(AB)+n(BC)+n(CA)] + n(ABC)",
      "\\text{Number belonging to EXACTLY ONE set: } \\sum n(A) - 2\\sum n(A \\cap B) + 3 n(A \\cap B \\cap C)",
      "\\text{Number belonging to EXACTLY TWO sets: } \\sum n(A \\cap B) - 3 n(A \\cap B \\cap C)",
      "\\text{Number belonging to AT LEAST TWO sets: } \\sum n(A \\cap B) - 2 n(A \\cap B \\cap C)"
    ],
