    "kind": "definition",
    "summary": "Mathematical foundation of relational databases defined by E.F. Codd. Relation: Table of values. Tuple: Row. Attribute: Column. Domain: Set of permitted atomic values. Arity / Degree: Number of attributes (columns). Cardinality: Number of tuples (rows). Relations are sets of tuples (no duplicate tuples allowed; row order is immaterial).",
    "formula": "\\text{Degree (Arity)} = \\#\\text{Columns}, \\quad \\text{Cardinality} = \\#\\text{Rows}",
    "keyFormulae": [
      "\\text{Cartesian Product } R(A, B) \\times S(C, D, E): \\text{Degree} = \\text{Deg}(R) + \\text{Deg}(S) = 2 + 3 = 5",
      "\\text{Cartesian Product Cardinality} = \\text{Card}(R) \\times \\text{Card}(S) = |R| \\times |S|",
      "\\text{Union Compatible: Two relations must have SAME degree and corresponding attributes from same domain}"
    ],
    "complexity": "Relational Set Semantics: Pure mathematical relation contains NO duplicate tuples",
    "codeSnippet": "-- In Relational Algebra, duplicates are automatically eliminated:\n-- \u03c0_{DeptName}(Employee) returns distinct department names.\n-- In SQL, SELECT DeptName FROM Employee preserves duplicates by default (Multiset semantics).\n-- Use SELECT DISTINCT DeptName FROM Employee for true set semantics.",
    "imageUrl": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 460 120\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect width=\"460\" height=\"120\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#0F172A\"/><rect x=\"25\" y=\"20\" width=\"190\" height=\"75\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#1E293B\" stroke=\"#38BDF8\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"45\" fill=\"#38BDF8\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Degree / Arity</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"70\" fill=\"#CBD5E1\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Number of Columns</text><rect x=\"245\" y=\"20\" width=\"190\" height=\"75\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#1E293B\" stroke=\"#22C55E\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"340\" y=\"45\" fill=\"#22C55E\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Cardinality</text><text x=\"340\" y=\"70\" fill=\"#CBD5E1\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Number of Rows (Tuples)</text></svg>",
    "commonTraps": [
      "Relational Algebra operates on SETS (no duplicates); SQL operates on MULTISETS / BAGS by default (preserves duplicates unless `DISTINCT` is specified).",
      "Degree of $R \\times S = \\text{Deg}(R) + \\text{Deg}(S)$; Cardinality of $R \\times S = |R| \\times |S|$."
    ],
