    "id": "c-dbms-relational-algebra",
    "subjectId": "DBMS",
    "chapterId": "dbms-relational-algebra",
    "label": "Relational Algebra: Fundamental Operators (Select, Project, Product, Set)",
    "name": "Relational Algebra Fundamentals",
    "category": "Relational Algebra & SQL",
    "kind": "definition",
    "summary": "Procedural query language working on relations. 6 Fundamental Operators: 1. Selection ($\\sigma_p(R)$: filters rows satisfying predicate $p$); 2. Projection ($\\pi_L(R)$: selects columns in list $L$, eliminates duplicate rows); 3. Cartesian Product ($R \\times S$: pairs every row of $R$ with every row of $S$); 4. Set Union ($R \\cup S$); 5. Set Difference ($R - S$); 6. Rename ($\\rho_{S(A_1, \\dots, A_n)}(R)$).",
    "formula": "\\text{Selection: } \\sigma_{\\text{Salary} > 50000}(\\text{Emp}), \\quad \\text{Projection: } \\pi_{\\text{Name, Salary}}(\\text{Emp})",
    "keyFormulae": [
      "\\text{Selection Cardinality: } 0 \\le |\\sigma_p(R)| \\le |R|",
      "\\text{Projection Cardinality: } 1 \\le |\\pi_L(R)| \\le |R| \\; (\\text{if } L \\text{ contains a candidate key, } |\\pi_L(R)| = |R|)",
      "\\text{Union & Difference require UNION COMPATIBILITY (Same degree and matching attribute domains)}",
      "\\text{Commutativity: } \\sigma_{p_1}(\\sigma_{p_2}(R)) \\equiv \\sigma_{p_2}(\\sigma_{p_1}(R)) \\equiv \\sigma_{p_1 \\land p_2}(R)"
    ],
    "complexity": "Selection: $O(|R|)$ table scan, Cartesian Product: $O(|R| \\times |S|)$",
    "codeSnippet": "-- Relational Algebra to SQL Equivalents:\n-- \u03c3_{Age >= 18}(Students)   <==> SELECT * FROM Students WHERE Age >= 18;\n-- \u03c0_{Name, Age}(Students)   <==> SELECT DISTINCT Name, Age FROM Students;\n-- R \u222a S                     <==> SELECT * FROM R UNION SELECT * FROM S;\n-- R - S                     <==> SELECT * FROM R EXCEPT SELECT * FROM S;",
    "imageUrl": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 460 130\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect width=\"460\" height=\"130\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#0F172A\"/><rect x=\"25\" y=\"20\" width=\"125\" height=\"85\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#1E293B\" stroke=\"#38BDF8\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"87\" y=\"45\" fill=\"#38BDF8\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Selection \u03c3_p</text><text x=\"87\" y=\"72\" fill=\"#CBD5E1\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Filters Rows (Horizontal)</text><rect x=\"165\" y=\"20\" width=\"125\" height=\"85\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#1E293B\" stroke=\"#22C55E\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"227\" y=\"45\" fill=\"#22C55E\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Projection \u03c0_L</text><text x=\"227\" y=\"72\" fill=\"#CBD5E1\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Filters Cols (Vertical)</text><rect x=\"305\" y=\"20\" width=\"130\" height=\"85\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#1E293B\" stroke=\"#EF4444\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"370\" y=\"45\" fill=\"#EF4444\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Product R \u00d7 S</text><text x=\"370\" y=\"72\" fill=\"#CBD5E1\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Degree = deg1 + deg2</text><text x=\"370\" y=\"90\" fill=\"#EF4444\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Card = |R| \u00d7 |S|</text></svg>",
    "commonTraps": [
      "In Relational Algebra, Projection $\\pi$ AUTOMATICALLY eliminates duplicate rows (unlike basic SQL `SELECT` which preserves duplicates).",
      "Set Intersection ($\\cap$) and Natural Join ($\\bowtie$) are DERIVED operators, NOT fundamental operators ($R \\cap S = R - (R - S)$)."
    ],
