    "kind": "algorithm",
    "summary": "Combining rows from two or more tables based on a related column: 1. `INNER JOIN` (matches present in both tables); 2. `LEFT OUTER JOIN` (all rows from left + matched right rows, padded with NULL if no match); 3. `RIGHT OUTER JOIN`; 4. `FULL OUTER JOIN` (all rows from both tables); 5. `CROSS JOIN` (Cartesian product); 6. `SELF JOIN` (table joined with itself using aliases).",
    "formula": "\\text{Cardinality Bound: } 0 \\le |A \\bowtie_{\\text{INNER}} B| \\le |A| \\times |B|, \\quad |A \\; \\text{LEFT JOIN} \\; B| \\ge |A|",
    "keyFormulae": [
      "\\text{Left Outer Join: } A \\; \\text{LOJ} \\; B = (A \\bowtie B) \\cup (A - \\pi_{\\text{Attrs}(A)}(A \\bowtie B)) \\times \\{\\text{NULL}\\}",
      "\\text{Full Outer Join: } A \\; \\text{FOJ} \\; B = (A \\; \\text{LOJ} \\; B) \\cup (A \\; \\text{ROJ} \\; B)",
      "\\text{Self Join: Requires table aliases (e.g. } \\texttt{Employee E1 JOIN Employee E2 ON E1.ManagerId = E2.EmpId})"
    ],
