    "label": "SQL GROUP BY, HAVING vs WHERE & Aggregate Functions",
    "name": "SQL Aggregation & Grouping",
    "category": "Relational Algebra & SQL",
    "kind": "algorithm",
    "summary": "Data aggregation pipeline. `WHERE` filters individual rows BEFORE grouping. `GROUP BY` partitions rows into groups sharing identical values on grouping columns. `HAVING` filters aggregated groups AFTER grouping. Aggregate functions (`COUNT`, `SUM`, `AVG`, `MIN`, `MAX`) ignore NULLs (except `COUNT(*)`).",
    "formula": "\\text{SQL Logical Execution: } \\text{FROM} \\to \\text{WHERE} \\to \\text{GROUP BY} \\to \\text{HAVING} \\to \\text{SELECT} \\to \\text{ORDER BY}",
    "keyFormulae": [
      "\\texttt{COUNT(*)}: \\text{Counts ALL rows in group, including rows with NULL values}",
      "\\texttt{COUNT(column)}: \\text{Counts only NON-NULL values in specified column}",
      "\\texttt{AVG(column)} = \\frac{\\sum \\text{Non-Null values}}{\\text{COUNT(column)}} \\; (\\text{Divisor excludes NULL rows})",
      "\\text{Select Clause Rule: Every non-aggregate column in SELECT must appear in GROUP BY list}"
    ],
    "complexity": "Grouping Complexity: $O(N \\log N)$ with Sorting or $O(N)$ with Hash Aggregation",
    "codeSnippet": "-- Finding Departments with Average Salary > 60000:\nSELECT DeptId, COUNT(*) AS EmpCount, AVG(Salary) AS AvgSal\nFROM Employee\nWHERE Status = 'ACTIVE'       -- 1. Row filter before group\nGROUP BY DeptId               -- 2. Grouping\nHAVING COUNT(*) >= 5          -- 3. Group filter after aggregate\n   AND AVG(Salary) > 60000\nORDER BY AvgSal DESC;         -- 4. Final sorting",
    "imageUrl": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 460 130\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect width=\"460\" height=\"130\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#0F172A\"/><rect x=\"25\" y=\"20\" width=\"95\" height=\"85\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#1E293B\" stroke=\"#38BDF8\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"72\" y=\"45\" fill=\"#38BDF8\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">1. WHERE</text><text x=\"72\" y=\"72\" fill=\"#CBD5E1\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Filters Rows</text><text x=\"72\" y=\"90\" fill=\"#38BDF8\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Before Group</text><rect x=\"130\" y=\"20\" width=\"95\" height=\"85\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#1E293B\" stroke=\"#22C55E\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"177\" y=\"45\" fill=\"#22C55E\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2. GROUP BY</text><text x=\"177\" y=\"72\" fill=\"#CBD5E1\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Forms buckets</text><text x=\"177\" y=\"90\" fill=\"#22C55E\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\">by columns</text><rect x=\"235\" y=\"20\" width=\"95\" height=\"85\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#1E293B\" stroke=\"#F59E0B\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"282\" y=\"45\" fill=\"#F59E0B\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">3. HAVING</text><text x=\"282\" y=\"72\" fill=\"#CBD5E1\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Filters Groups</text><text x=\"282\" y=\"90\" fill=\"#F59E0B\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Aggregates OK</text><rect x=\"340\" y=\"20\" width=\"95\" height=\"85\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#1E293B\" stroke=\"#EF4444\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"387\" y=\"45\" fill=\"#EF4444\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">4. SELECT</text><text x=\"387\" y=\"72\" fill=\"#CBD5E1\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Emits results</text><text x=\"387\" y=\"90\" fill=\"#EF4444\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\">ORDER BY</text></svg>",
    "commonTraps": [
      "`WHERE` CANNOT contain aggregate functions (e.g. `WHERE AVG(Salary) > 50000` is ILLEGAL; use `HAVING AVG(Salary) > 50000`).",
      "`COUNT(*)` counts NULLs, but `COUNT(Salary)` SKIPS NULLs. If a table has 5 rows with 2 NULL salaries, `COUNT(*) = 5` while `COUNT(Salary) = 3`.",
      "`AVG(col)` divides by the count of NON-NULL rows (NOT total rows)."
    ],
