    "label": "SQL Nested & Correlated Subqueries (EXISTS, IN, ALL, ANY)",
    "name": "Nested & Correlated Subqueries",
    "category": "Relational Algebra & SQL",
    "kind": "algorithm",
    "summary": "Subqueries embedded inside other queries: 1. Non-Correlated (Subquery executes ONCE independently); 2. Correlated Subquery (Inner query references columns of outer query, re-executing for EVERY outer tuple); 3. Set Membership (`IN`, `NOT IN`); 4. Set Comparison (`> ALL`, `> ANY` / `SOME`); 5. Existence Test (`EXISTS`, `NOT EXISTS`).",
    "formula": "\\text{Correlated Subquery: Evaluated } O(|\\text{Outer}|) \\text{ times (Row-by-Row)}",
    "keyFormulae": [
      "> \\text{ALL}(S) \\implies > \\max(S) \\quad | \\quad < \\text{ALL}(S) \\implies < \\min(S)",
      "> \\text{ANY}(S) \\implies > \\min(S) \\quad | \\quad < \\text{ANY}(S) \\implies < \\max(S)",
      "\\texttt{EXISTS}(Q): \\text{Returns TRUE if } Q \\text{ returns AT LEAST 1 row (Terminates on first match)}",
      "\\texttt{NOT IN} \\text{ with ANY NULL in subquery } \\implies \\text{Evaluates to UNKNOWN, returning ZERO rows!}"
    ],
    "complexity": "Query Optimizer: Transforms correlated subqueries into Joins via decorrelation",
    "codeSnippet": "-- Finding 2nd Highest Salary in SQL:\nSELECT MAX(Salary) FROM Employee \nWHERE Salary < (SELECT MAX(Salary) FROM Employee);\n\n-- Correlated Subquery: Employees earning above their Department Average:\nSELECT E.EmpName, E.Salary, E.DeptId\nFROM Employee E\nWHERE E.Salary > (\n    SELECT AVG(Salary) FROM Employee \n    WHERE DeptId = E.DeptId -- Outer correlation\n);",
    "imageUrl": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 460 120\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect width=\"460\" height=\"120\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#0F172A\"/><rect x=\"25\" y=\"20\" width=\"190\" height=\"75\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#1E293B\" stroke=\"#38BDF8\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"45\" fill=\"#38BDF8\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">&gt; ALL (Subquery)</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"70\" fill=\"#CBD5E1\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">&gt; MAX(Set)</text><rect x=\"245\" y=\"20\" width=\"190\" height=\"75\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#1E293B\" stroke=\"#22C55E\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"340\" y=\"45\" fill=\"#22C55E\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">&gt; ANY (Subquery)</text><text x=\"340\" y=\"70\" fill=\"#CBD5E1\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">&gt; MIN(Set)</text></svg>",
    "commonTraps": [
      "THE `NOT IN` NULL TRAP: If the subquery contains even a single `NULL` value, `x NOT IN (1, 2, NULL)` evaluates to `UNKNOWN`, and the query returns ZERO rows! Use `NOT EXISTS` instead.",
      "`> ALL (empty set)` evaluates to `TRUE` for all rows; `> ANY (empty set)` evaluates to `FALSE`."
    ],
