    "summary": "A decomposition of relation $R$ into $R_1, R_2, \\dots, R_k$ is Dependency Preserving if the union of functional dependencies enforceable locally on sub-relations is logically equivalent to the original set of dependencies: $(F_1 \\cup F_2 \\cup \\dots \\cup F_k)^+ = F^+$. Ensures integrity constraints can be enforced without expensive joins.",
