    "id": "c-dbms-conflict-serializability",
    "subjectId": "DBMS",
    "chapterId": "dbms-transactions",
    "label": "Conflict Serializability & Precedence Graph (Serialization Graph)",
    "name": "Conflict Serializability",
    "category": "Transactions & Concurrency Control",
    "kind": "algorithm",
    "summary": "A schedule $S$ is Conflict Serializable if it can be transformed into a serial schedule by swapping non-conflicting adjacent operations. Tested via Precedence Graph (Serialization Graph) $G = (V, E)$: nodes are transactions; directed edge $T_i \\to T_j$ if $T_i$ executes a conflicting operation BEFORE $T_j$. Schedule is conflict serializable IF AND ONLY IF graph is ACYCLIC.",
    "formula": "\\text{Schedule } S \\text{ is Conflict Serializable} \\iff \\text{Precedence Graph } G \\text{ has NO Cycles (Acyclic)}",
    "keyFormulae": [
      "\\text{Edge } T_i \\to T_j \\text{ drawn if: } R_i(X) < W_j(X) \\lor W_i(X) < R_j(X) \\lor W_i(X) < W_j(X)",
      "\\text{Equivalent Serial Order: Obtained via TOPOLOGICAL SORT of the Acyclic Precedence Graph}",
      "\\text{Number of Equivalent Serial Schedules: Number of valid topological sorts of } G",
      "\\text{Conflict Serializable Schedules } \\subset \\text{View Serializable Schedules}"
    ],
    "complexity": "Cycle Detection in Precedence Graph: $O(V + E)$ using DFS / Kahn's algorithm",
    "codeSnippet": "# Conflict Serializability Precedence Graph in Python\nfrom collections import defaultdict\ndef is_conflict_serializable(schedule_ops):\n    # schedule_ops = [('R', 1, 'A'), ('W', 2, 'A'), ('R', 2, 'B'), ...]\n    adj = defaultdict(set)\n    n = len(schedule_ops)\n    for i in range(n):\n        op1, t1, x1 = schedule_ops[i]\n        for j in range(i + 1, n):\n            op2, t2, x2 = schedule_ops[j]\n            if t1 != t2 and x1 == x2 and ('W' in (op1, op2)):\n                adj[t1].add(t2) # Directed Edge T1 -> T2\n    # Run standard DFS cycle detection on adj\n    return 'Acyclic -> Conflict Serializable'",
    "imageUrl": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 460 130\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect width=\"460\" height=\"130\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#0F172A\"/><circle cx=\"100\" cy=\"65\" r=\"18\" fill=\"#38BDF8\"/><text x=\"100\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#0F172A\">T1</text><circle cx=\"230\" cy=\"65\" r=\"18\" fill=\"#22C55E\"/><text x=\"230\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#0F172A\">T2</text><circle cx=\"360\" cy=\"65\" r=\"18\" fill=\"#EF4444\"/><text x=\"360\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#0F172A\">T3</text><line x1=\"118\" y1=\"65\" x2=\"210\" y2=\"65\" stroke=\"#38BDF8\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"248\" y1=\"65\" x2=\"340\" y2=\"65\" stroke=\"#22C55E\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"230\" y=\"110\" fill=\"#22C55E\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"monospace\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Acyclic Graph \u21d2 Conflict Serializable (T1 \u2192 T2 \u2192 T3)</text></svg>",
    "commonTraps": [
      "If a precedence graph contains a cycle (e.g. $T_1 \\to T_2$ and $T_2 \\to T_1$), the schedule is NOT conflict serializable.",
      "Topological sort gives the EXACT equivalent serial order(s). If multiple topological sorts exist, there are multiple equivalent serial schedules."
    ],
