    "id": "c-dbms-bplus-tree-calculations",
    "subjectId": "DBMS",
    "chapterId": "dbms-storage-indexing",
    "label": "B+ Tree Height, Node Count & Search Block Access Math",
    "name": "B+ Tree Calculations",
    "category": "Storage, Indexing & Recovery",
    "kind": "algorithm",
    "summary": "Master formulas for quantitative B+ Tree problems in GATE: Maximum/Minimum height for $N$ records, Number of leaf nodes $= \\lceil N / \\text{Keys per Leaf} \\rceil$, Number of root and internal nodes, and Disk I/O block accesses to retrieve a record ($h + 1$ block accesses).",
    "formula": "\\text{Max Height: } h_{\\max} = 1 + \\left\\lceil \\log_{\\lceil p/2 \\rceil} \\left( \\frac{\\#\\text{Leaves}}{2} \\right) \\right\\rceil, \\quad \\text{Block Accesses} = h + 1",
    "keyFormulae": [
      "\\text{Total Leaf Nodes } L = \\lceil N / \\text{Keys per Leaf} \\rceil",
      "\\text{Level } 1 \\text{ (Above Leaves) Nodes} = \\lceil L / p \\rceil \\quad (\\text{Min Nodes: divide by } p, \\; \\text{Max Nodes: divide by } \\lceil p/2 \\rceil)",
      "\\text{Search Cost for Equality Query: } h \\text{ (index nodes)} + 1 \\text{ (data block fetch)} = h + 1",
      "\\text{Search Cost if Data Records stored directly IN Leaf nodes: } h \\text{ block accesses}"
    ],
    "complexity": "Tree Height: Typically $h = 3 \\text{ or } 4$ even for hundreds of millions of records",
    "codeSnippet": "# B+ Tree Height and Block Access Calculator in Python\nimport math\ndef bplus_tree_height(n_records, p_internal, p_leaf, full=True):\n    keys_per_leaf = p_leaf if full else math.ceil(p_leaf / 2)\n    fanout = p_internal if full else math.ceil(p_internal / 2)\n    leaves = math.ceil(n_records / keys_per_leaf)\n    # Height counting from root (level 1) down to leaf\n    height = 1\n    nodes = leaves\n    while nodes > 1:\n        height += 1\n        nodes = math.ceil(nodes / fanout)\n    return height, leaves",
