    "id": "c-toc-deterministic-pda-dcfl",
    "subjectId": "TOC",
    "chapterId": "toc-pushdown-automata",
    "label": "Deterministic PDA (DPDA) & Deterministic CFLs (DCFLs)",
    "name": "DPDA & DCFLs",
    "category": "Context-Free Languages & Pushdown Automata",
    "kind": "definition",
    "summary": "DPDA: PDA where for every state $q \\in Q$ and stack top $Z \\in \\Gamma$: 1. $|\\delta(q, a, Z)| \\le 1$ for all $a \\in \\Sigma \\cup \\{\\epsilon\\}$; 2. If $\\delta(q, \\epsilon, Z) \\ne \\emptyset$, then $\\delta(q, a, Z) = \\emptyset$ for ALL $a \\in \\Sigma$ (no simultaneous $\\epsilon$ and input moves). DCFL: Languages accepted by DPDA via final state. Strict hierarchy: $\\text{REG} \\subsetneq \\text{DCFL} \\subsetneq \\text{CFL}$.",
    "formula": "\\text{Strict Containment: } \\text{Regular} \\subsetneq \\text{DCFL} \\subsetneq \\text{CFL}",
    "keyFormulae": [
      "\\text{Classic DCFLs: } a^n b^n, \\; a^n b^{2n}, \\; w c w^R \\; (\\text{Marked Palindromes with center marker } c)",
      "\\text{Classic Non-Deterministic CFLs (CFL - DCFL): } w w^R \\; (\\text{Unmarked Palindromes}), \\; \\{ a^i b^j c^k \\mid i=j \\lor j=k \\}",
      "\\text{DCFL Complement Theorem: DCFLs are CLOSED under Complement! (unlike general CFLs)}",
      "\\text{Every DCFL has an UNAMBIGUOUS grammar (DCFL } \\implies \\text{Unambiguous CFL)}"
    ],
    "complexity": "Parsing: DPDA languages correspond exactly to LR(k) / LR(1) parsable grammars in $O(n)$ time",
    "codeSnippet": "-- DCFL vs Non-DCFL Examples:\n-- L1 = {w c w^R | w in {0, 1}*} --> DCFL (Deterministic match on marker 'c')\n-- L2 = {w w^R | w in {0, 1}*}   --> CFL, but NOT DCFL (Must guess center non-deterministically!)",
    "imageUrl": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 460 120\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect width=\"460\" height=\"120\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#0F172A\"/><circle cx=\"230\" cy=\"65\" r=\"52\" fill=\"#1E293B\" stroke=\"#EF4444\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"230\" y=\"24\" fill=\"#EF4444\" font-size=\"10\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">CFL (NPDA)</text><circle cx=\"230\" cy=\"70\" r=\"36\" fill=\"#1E293B\" stroke=\"#F59E0B\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"230\" y=\"45\" fill=\"#F59E0B\" font-size=\"9\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">DCFL (DPDA)</text><circle cx=\"230\" cy=\"78\" r=\"18\" fill=\"#38BDF8\"/><text x=\"230\" y=\"82\" fill=\"#0F172A\" font-size=\"8\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">REG</text></svg>",
    "commonTraps": [
      "$w c w^R$ (marked center) is a DCFL; $w w^R$ (unmarked center) is a CFL but NOT a DCFL (requires non-deterministic guessing of center point).",
      "DCFLs are CLOSED under Complement, but general CFLs are NOT closed under complement."
    ],
