    "kind": "definition",
    "summary": "Church-Turing Thesis: Any real-world algorithm or effective computation can be simulated by a Turing Machine (philosophical thesis, not a provable mathematical theorem). Universal Turing Machine (UTM): A single fixed TM $U$ that takes as input the encoding $\\langle M \\rangle$ of any TM $M$ and input string $w$, and simulates $M$ executing on $w$: $U(\\langle M, w \\rangle) = M(w)$.",
    "formula": "U(\\langle M, w \\rangle) = M(w) \\quad (\\text{Universal Turing Machine: Programmable General-Purpose Computer})",
