    "label": "Recursive (REC / Decidable) vs Recursively Enumerable (RE)",
    "name": "Recursive vs RE Languages",
    "category": "Turing Machines & Computability Theory",
    "kind": "definition",
    "summary": "Classification of Turing-computable languages: 1. Recursive (REC / Decidable / Turing-Decidable): Accepted by a Turing Machine that is GUARANTEED TO HALT on every input string (accepts if $w \\in L$, rejects if $w \\notin L$); 2. Recursively Enumerable (RE / Semi-Decidable / Turing-Recognizable): Accepted by a TM that halts and accepts if $w \\in L$, but MAY LOOP FOREVER if $w \\notin L$.",
    "formula": "\\text{REC (Decidable)} = \\text{Halting TM (Decider)} \\quad | \\quad \\text{RE (Semi-Decidable)} = \\text{General TM (May Loop)}",
    "keyFormulae": [
      "\\text{Language Hierarchy: } \\text{Regular} \\subsetneq \\text{CFL} \\subsetneq \\text{CSL} \\subsetneq \\text{REC (Decidable)} \\subsetneq \\text{RE (Turing Recognizable)}",
      "\\text{Halting Property: For REC languages, TM NEVER loops infinitely}",
      "\\text{Semi-Decision for RE: If } w \\in L \\implies \\text{TM halts in YES}; \\; \\text{If } w \\notin L \\implies \\text{TM halts in NO OR LOOPS FOREVER}"
    ],
    "complexity": "Halting Guarantee: REC deciders terminate in finite steps on all inputs",
    "codeSnippet": "# Decider vs Recognizer in Python\ndef rec_decider(w):\n    if is_valid(w): return 'ACCEPT'\n    else: return 'REJECT' # Guaranteed to return in finite time\n\ndef re_recognizer(w):\n    if is_valid(w): return 'ACCEPT'\n    else: \n        while True: pass # May loop forever on rejection!",
    "imageUrl": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 460 120\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect width=\"460\" height=\"120\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#0F172A\"/><rect x=\"25\" y=\"20\" width=\"190\" height=\"75\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#1E293B\" stroke=\"#22C55E\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"45\" fill=\"#22C55E\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">REC (Decidable)</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"70\" fill=\"#CBD5E1\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Halts on ALL inputs (Yes/No)</text><rect x=\"245\" y=\"20\" width=\"190\" height=\"75\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#1E293B\" stroke=\"#F59E0B\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"340\" y=\"45\" fill=\"#F59E0B\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">RE (Semi-Decidable)</text><text x=\"340\" y=\"70\" fill=\"#CBD5E1\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Halts on Yes, May Loop on No</text></svg>",
