    "id": "c-toc-re-complement-theorems",
    "subjectId": "TOC",
    "chapterId": "toc-computability",
    "label": "Complement Theorems for RE and REC Languages",
    "name": "RE Complement Theorems",
    "category": "Turing Machines & Computability Theory",
    "kind": "theorem",
    "summary": "Fundamental duality theorems: 1. A language $L$ is Recursive (Decidable) IF AND ONLY IF both $L$ and its complement $\\bar{L}$ are Recursively Enumerable ($L \\in \\text{REC} \\iff L \\in \\text{RE} \\land \\bar{L} \\in \\text{RE}$); 2. If $L \\in \\text{RE} - \\text{REC}$ (strictly RE and undecidable), then its complement $\\bar{L}$ is GUARANTEED NOT to be RE ($\\bar{L} \\notin \\text{RE}$).",
    "formula": "L \\in \\text{REC} \\iff (L \\in \\text{RE} \\land \\bar{L} \\in \\text{RE})",
    "keyFormulae": [
      "\\text{Theorem 1: } L \\in \\text{REC} \\iff L \\in \\text{RE} \\land \\bar{L} \\in \\text{RE}",
      "\\text{Theorem 2: If } L \\in \\text{RE} - \\text{REC} \\implies \\bar{L} \\notin \\text{RE} \\; (\\bar{L} \\text{ is strictly NON-RE})",
      "\\text{Theorem 3: If } L_1, L_2 \\in \\text{REC} \\implies L_1 \\cup L_2, L_1 \\cap L_2, \\bar{L}_1 \\in \\text{REC} \\; (\\text{REC closed under Boolean ops})",
      "\\text{Theorem 4: RE is CLOSED under } \\cup \\text{ and } \\cap, \\text{ but NOT closed under Complement!}"
    ],
    "complexity": "Proof Construction: Run $M_L$ and $M_{\\bar{L}}$ in parallel (dovetailing) until one halts",
    "codeSnippet": "# Parallel Dovetailing Simulation proving L in REC if L and L_bar in RE in Python\ndef decide_rec(w, tm_L, tm_Lbar):\n    step = 0\n    while True:\n        step += 1\n        if tm_L.run_steps(w, step) == 'ACCEPT': return 'ACCEPT (w in L)'\n        if tm_Lbar.run_steps(w, step) == 'ACCEPT': return 'REJECT (w in L_bar)'",
    "imageUrl": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 460 120\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect width=\"460\" height=\"120\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#0F172A\"/><rect x=\"25\" y=\"20\" width=\"190\" height=\"75\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#1E293B\" stroke=\"#22C55E\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"45\" fill=\"#22C55E\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">L \u2208 RE \u2227 L_bar \u2208 RE</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"70\" fill=\"#22C55E\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">\u21d2 L is REC (Decidable)</text><rect x=\"245\" y=\"20\" width=\"190\" height=\"75\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#1E293B\" stroke=\"#EF4444\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"340\" y=\"45\" fill=\"#EF4444\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">L \u2208 RE - REC</text><text x=\"340\" y=\"70\" fill=\"#EF4444\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">\u21d2 L_bar is NOT RE</text></svg>",
    "commonTraps": [
      "If $L$ is RE and undecidable (e.g. Halting Problem $HALT_{TM}$), then $\\bar{L}$ CANNOT BE RE (if it were RE, $L$ would become decidable!).",
      "RE is closed under Union and Intersection, but NOT closed under Complement or Set Difference."
    ],
