    "kind": "theorem",
    "summary": "Space complexity measures tape cells scanned during computation. $\\text{SPACE}(f(n))$: deterministic space $f(n)$, $\\text{NSPACE}(f(n))$: non-deterministic space. PSPACE is class of problems solvable in polynomial space. Savitch's Theorem: Any non-deterministic space $f(n)$ can be simulated deterministically in $O(f^2(n))$ space. Hence $\\text{PSPACE} = \\text{NPSPACE}$.",
    "formula": "\\text{Savitch's Theorem: } \\text{NSPACE}(f(n)) \\subseteq \\text{SPACE}(f^2(n)) \\implies \\text{PSPACE} = \\text{NPSPACE}",
