    "id": "c-coa-instruction-format",
    "subjectId": "Computer Organization & Architecture",
    "chapterId": "coa-instruction-set",
    "label": "Instruction Formats & Expanding Opcode Technique",
    "name": "Instruction Formats",
    "category": "Instruction Formats & Addressing Modes",
    "kind": "definition",
    "summary": "An instruction consists of an Opcode (operation to perform) and Operands/Addresses. Instructions can have 3, 2, 1 (Accumulator), or 0 (Stack) addresses. Expanding Opcode allows variable-length opcodes to maximize instruction variety in a fixed instruction word size.",
    "formula": "\\text{Expanding Opcode Unused Pattern: } N_{\\text{new}} = (\\text{Unused patterns in previous tier}) \\times 2^k",
    "keyFormulae": [
      "\\text{Instruction Word Size} = \\text{Opcode bits} + \\sum \\text{Address bits}",
      "\\text{Address bits for } N \\text{ words in memory: } k = \\log_2 N",
      "\\text{Register address bits for } R \\text{ registers: } r = \\log_2 R",
      "\\text{Expanding Opcode: If } 2^n - m \\text{ opcodes are unused in tier 1, tier 2 can have } (2^n - m) \\times 2^k \\text{ opcodes}"
    ],
    "complexity": "Encoding: Maximizes code density within fixed 16/32/64-bit instruction words",
    "codeSnippet": "# Expanding Opcode Capacity Calculator in Python\ndef expanding_opcode(word_bits, reg_bits, n_3addr, n_2addr):\n    # 3-address: Opcode + R1 + R2 + R3\n    op3_bits = word_bits - 3 * reg_bits\n    max_3addr = 2 ** op3_bits\n    unused_3 = max_3addr - n_3addr\n    # 2-address: Opcode + R1 + R2 (Opcode expands by reg_bits)\n    max_2addr = unused_3 * (2 ** reg_bits)\n    unused_2 = max_2addr - n_2addr\n    # 1-address: Opcode expands by another reg_bits\n    max_1addr = unused_2 * (2 ** reg_bits)\n    return {'max_2addr': max_2addr, 'max_1addr': max_1addr}",
    "imageUrl": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 460 130\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect width=\"460\" height=\"130\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#0F172A\"/><rect x=\"25\" y=\"20\" width=\"90\" height=\"35\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#EF4444\"/><text x=\"70\" y=\"42\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" font-size=\"10\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Opcode (4)</text><rect x=\"120\" y=\"20\" width=\"95\" height=\"35\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#38BDF8\"/><text x=\"167\" y=\"42\" fill=\"#0F172A\" font-size=\"10\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Reg 1 (4)</text><rect x=\"220\" y=\"20\" width=\"95\" height=\"35\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#38BDF8\"/><text x=\"267\" y=\"42\" fill=\"#0F172A\" font-size=\"10\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Reg 2 (4)</text><rect x=\"320\" y=\"20\" width=\"95\" height=\"35\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#38BDF8\"/><text x=\"367\" y=\"42\" fill=\"#0F172A\" font-size=\"10\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Reg 3 (4)</text><text x=\"230\" y=\"85\" fill=\"#22C55E\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"monospace\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">16-bit 3-Address Instruction Word</text><text x=\"230\" y=\"105\" fill=\"#F59E0B\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Unused 3-address opcodes expand into 2-address opcodes</text></svg>",
    "commonTraps": [
      "Word-addressable vs Byte-addressable: If memory is 16-bit word addressable, 64 KB memory has $32\\text{K words} = 2^{15} \\implies 15$ address bits (NOT 16 bits).",
      "Expanding opcode tree must NOT allocate all $2^n$ opcodes in the first tier, or zero opcodes remain for subsequent tiers."
    ],
