    "name": "2's Complement & Overflow",
    "category": "Computer Arithmetic",
    "kind": "definition",
    "summary": "Representation of signed integers in computer hardware. $n$-bit 2's complement range is $[-2^{n-1}, +2^{n-1} - 1]$. Has unique representation for zero ($0$). Overflow occurs during addition of two numbers with the same sign when the result has the opposite sign.",
    "formula": "\\text{Range of } n\\text{-bit 2's Complement: } -2^{n-1} \\le X \\le 2^{n-1} - 1",
    "keyFormulae": [
      "\\text{2's Complement of } X: 2^n - X = \\overline{X} + 1",
      "\\text{Overflow Condition: } V = C_{\\text{in}} \\oplus C_{\\text{out}} \\quad (C_{\\text{in}} = \\text{carry into MSB}, \\; C_{\\text{out}} = \\text{carry out of MSB})",
      "\\text{Sign Extension: To convert } n\\text{-bit to } m\\text{-bit } (m > n), \\text{ copy sign bit to all new higher-order bit positions}"
    ],
    "complexity": "Hardware Overflow Check: Single XOR gate delay ($O(1)$)",
    "codeSnippet": "# 2's Complement Overflow Detection in Python\ndef detect_overflow(a_msb, b_msb, sum_msb, c_in, c_out):\n    # Method 1: Carry XOR condition\n    overflow_xor = (c_in != c_out)\n    # Method 2: Sign rule: Positive + Positive = Negative OR Negative + Negative = Positive\n    overflow_sign = (a_msb == b_msb) and (a_msb != sum_msb)\n    return overflow_xor, overflow_sign",
    "imageUrl": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 460 120\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect width=\"460\" height=\"120\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#0F172A\"/><rect x=\"25\" y=\"20\" width=\"190\" height=\"75\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#1E293B\" stroke=\"#38BDF8\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"45\" fill=\"#38BDF8\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2's Complement Range</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"70\" fill=\"#CBD5E1\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">-2^(n-1) to +2^(n-1) - 1</text><rect x=\"245\" y=\"20\" width=\"190\" height=\"75\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#1E293B\" stroke=\"#EF4444\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"340\" y=\"45\" fill=\"#EF4444\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Overflow Flag V</text><text x=\"340\" y=\"70\" fill=\"#CBD5E1\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">V = C_in \u2295 C_out</text></svg>",
    "commonTraps": [
      "Adding a positive number and a negative number CAN NEVER produce an overflow.",
      "In 8-bit 2's complement, $-128$ ($10000000_2$) CANNOT be negated because $+128$ is outside the representable range $[-128, +127]$ (negating $-128$ yields $-128$!).",
      "Overflow flag $V$ is relevant ONLY for signed arithmetic; Carry flag $C$ is relevant for unsigned arithmetic."
    ],
