    "id": "c-coa-booth-algorithm",
    "subjectId": "Computer Organization & Architecture",
    "chapterId": "coa-arithmetic",
    "label": "Booth's Multiplication Algorithm for Signed Numbers",
    "name": "Booth's Multiplication",
    "category": "Computer Arithmetic",
    "kind": "algorithm",
    "summary": "Multiplies signed 2's complement integers by encoding blocks of consecutive 1s. Inspects 2-bit window $(Q_0, Q_{-1})$: $01 \\to A = A + M$ (beginning of 1s string), $10 \\to A = A - M$ (end of 1s string), $00 / 11 \\to \\text{No op}$. Followed by Arithmetic Shift Right on $[A, Q, Q_{-1}]$.",
    "formula": "\\text{Booth Recoding Table: } (Q_0, Q_{-1}) \\implies 01: +M, \\quad 10: -M, \\quad 00/11: 0",
    "keyFormulae": [
      "\\text{Best Case (Fewest Add/Sub operations): Multiplier has long consecutive blocks of 0s or 1s (e.g. } 00001111_2)",
      "\\text{Worst Case (Maximum Add/Sub operations): Multiplier is alternating } 01010101_2 \\text{ or } 10101010_2 \\implies n \\text{ operations for } n \\text{ bits}",
      "\\text{Arithmetic Shift Right preserves the sign bit of Accumulator } A"
    ],
    "complexity": "Cycles: Exactly $n$ iterations for $n$-bit multiplier ($n$ shifts, at most $n$ additions/subtractions)",
    "codeSnippet": "# Booth's Recoding in Python\ndef count_booth_operations(multiplier_bits):\n    # multiplier_bits = '01010101'\n    extended = multiplier_bits + '0' # Append Q_-1 = 0\n    add_sub_count = 0\n    for i in range(len(multiplier_bits)-1, -1, -1):\n        pair = extended[i] + extended[i+1]\n        if pair in ['01', '10']:\n            add_sub_count += 1\n    return add_sub_count",
    "imageUrl": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 460 120\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect width=\"460\" height=\"120\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#0F172A\"/><rect x=\"25\" y=\"20\" width=\"95\" height=\"75\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#1E293B\" stroke=\"#22C55E\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"72\" y=\"45\" fill=\"#22C55E\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">01</text><text x=\"72\" y=\"72\" fill=\"#CBD5E1\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">A = A + M</text><rect x=\"130\" y=\"20\" width=\"95\" height=\"75\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#1E293B\" stroke=\"#EF4444\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"177\" y=\"45\" fill=\"#EF4444\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">10</text><text x=\"177\" y=\"72\" fill=\"#CBD5E1\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">A = A - M</text><rect x=\"235\" y=\"20\" width=\"95\" height=\"75\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#1E293B\" stroke=\"#38BDF8\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"282\" y=\"45\" fill=\"#38BDF8\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">00 / 11</text><text x=\"282\" y=\"72\" fill=\"#CBD5E1\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Shift Only</text><rect x=\"340\" y=\"20\" width=\"95\" height=\"75\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#1E293B\" stroke=\"#F59E0B\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"387\" y=\"45\" fill=\"#F59E0B\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">ASH-R</text><text x=\"387\" y=\"72\" fill=\"#CBD5E1\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Preserve Sign</text></svg>",
    "commonTraps": [
      "$Q_{-1}$ is ALWAYS initialized to `0` at the start of Booth's algorithm.",
      "Worst-case multiplier for Booth's algorithm is alternating bits ($01010101_2$), which requires $n$ additions/subtractions.",
      "The shift step MUST be an ARITHMETIC shift right (sign-extending $A$), not a logical shift."
    ],
