    "id": "c-coa-restoring-nonrestoring",
    "subjectId": "Computer Organization & Architecture",
    "chapterId": "coa-arithmetic",
    "label": "Integer Division: Restoring vs Non-Restoring Division",
    "name": "Integer Division Algorithms",
    "category": "Computer Arithmetic",
    "kind": "algorithm",
    "summary": "Hardware algorithms for unsigned binary integer division ($Q = \\text{Dividend} / \\text{Divisor}$, $A = \\text{Remainder}$). Restoring Division subtracts divisor $M$; if $A < 0$, it restores $A = A + M$ and sets $q_0 = 0$. Non-Restoring Division skips restoration by adding $M$ in the next step when $A < 0$.",
    "formula": "\\text{Non-Restoring Step: If } A \\ge 0 \\implies \\text{Shift Left, } A = A - M; \\quad \\text{If } A < 0 \\implies \\text{Shift Left, } A = A + M",
    "keyFormulae": [
      "\\text{Restoring Division: Shift Left } [A, Q] \\to A = A - M; \\; \\text{If } A < 0 \\implies A = A + M \\text{ and } q_0 = 0; \\; \\text{else } q_0 = 1",
      "\\text{Non-Restoring Division: Avoids redundant add back, cutting worst-case cycles in half}",
      "\\text{Non-Restoring Final Correction: If final } A < 0, \\text{ perform } A = A + M \\text{ to restore true positive remainder}"
    ],
    "complexity": "Restoring: Up to $2n$ additions/subtractions; Non-restoring: Exactly $n$ arithmetic operations",
    "codeSnippet": "# Non-Restoring Division Simulator in Python\ndef non_restoring_divide(dividend, divisor, n_bits):\n    A = 0; Q = dividend; M = divisor\n    for _ in range(n_bits):\n        if A >= 0:\n            A = (A << 1) | ((Q >> (n_bits - 1)) & 1)\n            Q = (Q << 1) & ((1 << n_bits) - 1)\n            A = A - M\n        else:\n            A = (A << 1) | ((Q >> (n_bits - 1)) & 1)\n            Q = (Q << 1) & ((1 << n_bits) - 1)\n            A = A + M\n        if A >= 0: Q |= 1\n        else: Q |= 0\n    if A < 0: A = A + M # Final correction\n    return Q, A # Quotient, Remainder",
    "imageUrl": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 460 120\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect width=\"460\" height=\"120\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#0F172A\"/><rect x=\"25\" y=\"20\" width=\"190\" height=\"75\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#1E293B\" stroke=\"#38BDF8\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"45\" fill=\"#38BDF8\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Restoring Division</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"70\" fill=\"#CBD5E1\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">If A &lt; 0, add back M (Slow)</text><rect x=\"245\" y=\"20\" width=\"190\" height=\"75\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#1E293B\" stroke=\"#22C55E\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"340\" y=\"45\" fill=\"#22C55E\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Non-Restoring</text><text x=\"340\" y=\"70\" fill=\"#CBD5E1\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Alternates +/- M (Fast)</text></svg>",
    "commonTraps": [
      "In Non-Restoring division, if the remainder $A$ is NEGATIVE at the very end of all $n$ iterations, ONE final restoration ($A = A + M$) MUST be performed.",
      "Quotient bits are set to `1` when $A \\ge 0$, and `0` when $A < 0$."
    ],
