    "summary": "Hill's 3Cs model classifies cache misses into: 1. Compulsory (Cold start: first reference to a block); 2. Capacity (Cache is too small to hold all working set blocks); 3. Conflict (Collision: multiple blocks map to the same set/line). 4th C in multiprocessors: Coherence misses (invalidation by other cores).",
    "formula": "\\text{Total Misses} = \\text{Compulsory} + \\text{Capacity} + \\text{Conflict} (+ \\text{Coherence})",
