    "label": "DMA Architecture, Cycle Stealing & Burst Mode",
    "name": "DMA Controller Architecture",
    "category": "I/O & Secondary Storage",
    "kind": "definition",
    "summary": "Direct Memory Access (DMA) offloads bulk data transfers between high-speed devices and RAM. The DMA controller acts as bus master. Operating Modes: 1. Cycle Stealing (DMA steals 1 bus cycle from CPU during instruction operand fetch); 2. Burst / Block Transfer (DMA retains bus for entire block).",
    "formula": "\\text{Cycle Stealing CPU Slowdown} = \\frac{\\text{DMA Transfer Rate (Bytes/sec)}}{\\text{Memory Bus Bandwidth (Bytes/sec)}} \\times 100\\%",
    "keyFormulae": [
      "\\text{DMA Bus Request (HRQ / HOLD) and Acknowledge (HLDA) handshake}",
      "\\text{Time to transfer block of } N \\text{ bytes in Burst Mode: } T_{\\text{setup}} + (N \\times T_{\\text{bus\\_cycle}})",
      "\\text{Cycle Stealing: CPU execution is delayed by 1 cycle for every byte transferred when both request memory bus}"
    ],
    "complexity": "CPU Utilization: Frees $> 95\\%$ of CPU cycles during massive disk/network transfers",
    "codeSnippet": "# DMA Cycle Stealing CPU Slowdown in Python\ndef dma_slowdown_percentage(device_speed_bps, bus_bandwidth_bps):\n    slowdown = (device_speed_bps / bus_bandwidth_bps) * 100.0\n    return slowdown\n# e.g. 2 MB/s device on 100 MB/s bus: 2% CPU slowdown",
    "imageUrl": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 460 120\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect width=\"460\" height=\"120\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#0F172A\"/><rect x=\"25\" y=\"20\" width=\"190\" height=\"75\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#1E293B\" stroke=\"#38BDF8\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"45\" fill=\"#38BDF8\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Cycle Stealing</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"70\" fill=\"#CBD5E1\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Steals 1 bus cycle at a time</text><rect x=\"245\" y=\"20\" width=\"190\" height=\"75\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#1E293B\" stroke=\"#22C55E\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"340\" y=\"45\" fill=\"#22C55E\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Burst Mode</text><text x=\"340\" y=\"70\" fill=\"#CBD5E1\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Transfers entire block continuously</text></svg>",
    "commonTraps": [
      "In Cycle Stealing, the CPU is NOT blocked unless it attempts to access the memory bus at the exact same clock cycle as the DMA controller.",
      "DMA controller must be initialized by the CPU with: Starting RAM Address, Word Count, and Control Command (Read/Write)."
    ],
