    "summary": "Bottom-up shift-reduce technique for Operator Grammars (Grammars with NO $\\epsilon$-productions and NO adjacent non-terminals $AB$). Defines three precedence relations between terminals: 1. $a \\lessdot b$ ($a$ yields precedence to $b$ $\\implies$ SHIFT); 2. $a \\doteq b$ ($a$ has same precedence as $b$); 3. $a \\gtrdot b$ ($a$ takes precedence over $b$ $\\implies$ REDUCE). Handle is bracketed between $\\lessdot$ and $\\gtrdot$.",
    "formula": "\\text{Operator Grammar: } A \\to \\epsilon \\text{ forbidden } \\land A \\to \\alpha BC \\beta \\text{ forbidden}",
    "keyFormulae": [
      "\\text{Shift Action: } a \\lessdot b \\implies \\text{Push } b \\text{ onto parsing stack}",
      "\\text{Reduce Action: } a \\gtrdot b \\implies \\text{Locate handle delimited by } \\lessdot \\dots \\gtrdot \\text{ and reduce}",
      "\\text{Precedence Function: Maps terminals to integers } f(a), g(b) \\text{ such that } a \\lessdot b \\iff f(a) < g(b)",
      "\\text{Operator precedence parsers can parse SOME ambiguous grammars (e.g. } E \\to E+E \\mid E*E \\mid id)"
    ],
    "complexity": "Operator Precedence Parsing: $O(N)$ linear time over expression tokens",
    "codeSnippet": "-- Operator Precedence Table for +, *, id, $:\n--        +       *       id      $\n-- +      .>      <\u00b7      <\u00b7      .>\n-- *      .>      .>      <\u00b7      .>\n-- id     .>      .>      ERR     .>\n-- $      <\u00b7      <\u00b7      <\u00b7      ACC",
