    "name": "Handles & Handle Pruning",
    "category": "Bottom-Up Parsing & LR Parsers",
    "kind": "definition",
    "summary": "Handle: Substring $\\beta$ of a right sentential form $\\gamma = \\alpha\\beta w$ matching the RHS of production $A \\to \\beta$ such that reducing $\\beta$ to $A$ produces the PREVIOUS right sentential form in the rightmost derivation ($S \\Rightarrow_{\\text{rm}}^* \\alpha A w \\Rightarrow_{\\text{rm}} \\alpha\\beta w$). Handle Pruning is the bottom-up process of repeatedly locating handles and reducing them to reach start symbol $S$.",
    "formula": "\\text{Handle: } (A \\to \\beta, \\; \\text{position of } \\beta) \\text{ in right sentential form } \\alpha\\beta w \\iff S \\Rightarrow_{\\text{rm}}^* \\alpha A w \\Rightarrow_{\\text{rm}} \\alpha\\beta w",
    "keyFormulae": [
      "\\text{Right Sentential Form: Sentential form derivable via Rightmost Derivation } (S \\Rightarrow_{\\text{rm}}^* \\gamma)",
      "\\text{Handle Property: In } \\alpha\\beta w, \\; w \\text{ consists EXCLUSIVELY of terminal symbols!}",
      "\\text{Unambiguous Grammars: Every right sentential form has EXACTLY ONE unique handle}",
      "\\text{LR Parsers: Deterministically locate the handle at the top of the stack using the LR DFA}"
    ],
    "complexity": "Handle Discovery: $O(1)$ table lookup in LR parsers",
    "codeSnippet": "-- Handle Pruning Example:\n-- Grammar: S -> a A b e, A -> A b c | b, B -> d\n-- Rightmost Derivation: S => a A b e => a A b c d e => a b b c d e\n-- Handle in 'a b b c d e': 'b' at index 2 (Reduce by A -> b)\n-- Next Sentential Form: 'a A b c d e', Handle: 'A b c' (Reduce by A -> A b c)\n-- Next: 'a A d e' ... continuing up to S!",
