    "id": "c-cd-lr0-items",
    "subjectId": "Compiler Design",
    "chapterId": "cd-bottom-up-parsing",
    "label": "LR(0) Items, Item Closure & GOTO Transition Function",
    "name": "LR(0) Automaton",
    "category": "Bottom-Up Parsing & LR Parsers",
    "kind": "algorithm",
    "summary": "Building block of LR parsers. An LR(0) item of grammar $G$ is a production with a dot '$\\cdot$' at some position on RHS (e.g. $A \\to \\alpha \\cdot \\beta$). Augmented Grammar adds $S' \\to S$. CLOSURE($I$): If $[A \\to \\alpha \\cdot B \\beta] \\in I$, add $[B \\to \\cdot \\gamma]$ for all $B \\to \\gamma$. $\\text{GOTO}(I, X) = \\text{CLOSURE}(\\{ [A \\to \\alpha X \\cdot \\beta] \\mid [A \\to \\alpha \\cdot X \\beta] \\in I \\})$.",
    "formula": "\\text{Item Count for production of length } k = k + 1 \\text{ LR(0) items}",
    "keyFormulae": [
      "\\text{Kernel Items: } S' \\to \\cdot S \\text{ and all items whose dot is NOT at the left end } (A \\to \\alpha \\cdot \\beta, \\alpha \\ne \\epsilon)",
      "\\text{Non-Kernel Items: Items with dot at the extreme left } (A \\to \\cdot \\gamma, \\gamma \\in (V \\cup T)^*)",
      "\\text{Reduce Item / Complete Item: Item with dot at the extreme right } (A \\to \\alpha \\cdot)",
      "\\text{Shift Item: Item with dot before a terminal } (A \\to \\alpha \\cdot a \\beta)"
    ],
    "complexity": "Canonical Collection Construction: Computes finite state automaton recognizing all viable prefixes",
    "codeSnippet": "# LR(0) Item Closure in Python\ndef lr0_closure(item_set, grammar):\n    closure = set(item_set)\n    changed = True\n    while changed:\n        changed = False\n        for lhs, rhs, dot_pos in list(closure):\n            if dot_pos < len(rhs) and rhs[dot_pos] in grammar.variables:\n                B = rhs[dot_pos]\n                for b_rhs in grammar.productions_for(B):\n                    new_item = (B, b_rhs, 0) # Dot at start: B -> . gamma\n                    if new_item not in closure:\n                        closure.add(new_item)\n                        changed = True\n    return closure",
    "imageUrl": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 460 120\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect width=\"460\" height=\"120\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#0F172A\"/><rect x=\"25\" y=\"20\" width=\"190\" height=\"75\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#1E293B\" stroke=\"#38BDF8\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"45\" fill=\"#38BDF8\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">CLOSURE(I)</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"70\" fill=\"#CBD5E1\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Expands dot before variable B</text><rect x=\"245\" y=\"20\" width=\"190\" height=\"75\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#1E293B\" stroke=\"#22C55E\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"340\" y=\"45\" fill=\"#22C55E\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">GOTO(I, X)</text><text x=\"340\" y=\"70\" fill=\"#CBD5E1\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Advances dot over symbol X</text></svg>",
    "commonTraps": [
      "Production of length $k$ (e.g. $A \\to XYZ$) produces EXACTLY $k+1 = 4$ distinct LR(0) items.",
      "An $\\epsilon$-production $A \\to \\epsilon$ has EXACTLY ONE item: $A \\to \\cdot$ (which is immediately a complete reduce item!)."
    ],
