    "id": "c-cd-slr1-parser",
    "subjectId": "Compiler Design",
    "chapterId": "cd-bottom-up-parsing",
    "label": "Simple LR (SLR(1)) Parser Table Construction & Rules",
    "name": "SLR(1) Parser",
    "category": "Bottom-Up Parsing & LR Parsers",
    "kind": "algorithm",
    "summary": "Uses the canonical collection of LR(0) items, but resolves reduce actions using 1-symbol lookahead from FOLLOW sets: 1. If $[A \\to \\alpha \\cdot a \\beta] \\in I_i$ and $\\text{GOTO}(I_i, a) = I_j$, set $\\text{ACTION}[i, a] = \\text{shift } j$; 2. If $[A \\to \\alpha \\cdot] \\in I_i$, set $\\text{ACTION}[i, a] = \\text{reduce } A \\to \\alpha$ for ALL $a \\in \\text{FOLLOW}(A)$; 3. If $[S' \\to S \\cdot] \\in I_i$, set $\\text{ACTION}[i, \\$] = \\text{accept}$.",
    "formula": "\\text{SLR(1) Reduce Action: If } [A \\to \\alpha \\cdot] \\in I_i \\implies \\text{ACTION}[i, a] = \\text{Reduce } (A \\to \\alpha) \\quad \\forall a \\in \\text{FOLLOW}(A)",
    "keyFormulae": [
      "\\text{SLR(1) Conflict 1 (Shift-Reduce): State contains } [A \\to \\alpha \\cdot a \\beta] \\text{ and } [B \\to \\gamma \\cdot] \\text{ with } a \\in \\text{FOLLOW}(B)",
      "\\text{SLR(1) Conflict 2 (Reduce-Reduce): State contains } [A \\to \\alpha \\cdot] \\text{ and } [B \\to \\beta \\cdot] \\text{ with } \\text{FOLLOW}(A) \\cap \\text{FOLLOW}(B) \\ne \\emptyset",
      "\\text{State Count: } |Q_{\\text{SLR(1)}}| = |Q_{\\text{LR(0)}}| \\; (\\text{Uses identical LR(0) automaton states})"
    ],
    "complexity": "Table Construction: $O(|Q_{\\text{LR0}}| \\cdot (|T| + |V|))$",
    "codeSnippet": "# SLR(1) Table Generator in Python\ndef construct_slr1_table(lr0_states, goto_table, follow_dict):\n    action = {}; goto = {}\n    for i, state in enumerate(lr0_states):\n        for item in state:\n            if is_shift_item(item):\n                a = item.next_symbol\n                if is_terminal(a): action[i, a] = ('shift', goto_table[i, a])\n            elif is_reduce_item(item):\n                A = item.lhs\n                for a in follow_dict[A]:\n                    action[i, a] = ('reduce', item.production)\n    return action, goto",
    "imageUrl": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 460 120\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect width=\"460\" height=\"120\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#0F172A\"/><rect x=\"25\" y=\"20\" width=\"190\" height=\"75\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#1E293B\" stroke=\"#38BDF8\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"45\" fill=\"#38BDF8\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">LR(0) Reduce</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"70\" fill=\"#EF4444\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Places reduce in ALL columns</text><rect x=\"245\" y=\"20\" width=\"190\" height=\"75\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#1E293B\" stroke=\"#22C55E\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"340\" y=\"45\" fill=\"#22C55E\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">SLR(1) Reduce</text><text x=\"340\" y=\"70\" fill=\"#22C55E\" font-size=\"10\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Places reduce ONLY in FOLLOW(A)</text></svg>",
    "commonTraps": [
      "In LR(0), reduce actions are placed in EVERY terminal column; In SLR(1), reduce actions are placed ONLY in columns $a \\in \\text{FOLLOW}(A)$.",
      "SLR(1) uses the EXACT same number of states as LR(0)."
    ],
