    "id": "c-cd-code-optimization",
    "subjectId": "Compiler Design",
    "chapterId": "cd-runtime-optimization",
    "label": "Code Optimization Techniques: Constant Folding, Propagation & Dead Code",
    "name": "Code Optimization Techniques",
    "category": "Runtime Environments & Code Optimization",
    "kind": "technique",
    "summary": "Transformations improving program execution speed and reducing memory footprint without altering program semantics. Principal Techniques: 1. Constant Folding (Compile-time evaluation of constant expressions, e.g. `3 + 5` $\\to$ `8`); 2. Constant Propagation (Replacing variables known to be constant with their values); 3. Common Subexpression Elimination (CSE); 4. Dead Code Elimination (Removing unreachable code or values never read).",
    "formula": "\\text{Optimization Rules: } \\text{Preserves Semantics} \\land \\text{Reduces Time/Space} \\land \\text{Compiles in Reasonable Time}",
    "keyFormulae": [
      "\\text{Constant Folding: } x = 3.14159 \\times 2 \\implies x = 6.28318 \\; (\\text{Zero runtime multiplications})",
      "\\text{Constant Propagation: } x = 14; \\dots y = x + 2 \\implies y = 14 + 2 = 16",
      "\\text{Common Subexpression Elimination: If } a = b + c \\text{ and } d = b + c \\text{ without intervening modifications } \\implies d = a",
      "\\text{Dead Code Elimination: If variable } t \\text{ is never used in any live path, delete } t = \\dots"
    ],
