    "id": "c-cd-dag-optimization",
    "subjectId": "Compiler Design",
    "chapterId": "cd-runtime-optimization",
    "label": "Directed Acyclic Graph (DAG) Representation of Basic Blocks",
    "name": "DAG Representation of Basic Blocks",
    "category": "Runtime Environments & Code Optimization",
    "kind": "algorithm",
    "summary": "Graphical data structure capturing local data dependencies within a basic block. Interior nodes represent operators labeled by operator symbols; Leaf nodes represent initial variable values / constants. Automatically detects: 1. Local Common Subexpressions (Reuses existing node instead of creating duplicates); 2. Dead Code (Unreferenced interior nodes); 3. Value numbering. Output gives optimal 3AC instruction order.",
    "formula": "\\text{DAG Node Reuse: If node } n = (\\text{op}, n_1, n_2) \\text{ exists } \\implies \\text{Attach new variable label to } n",
    "keyFormulae": [
      "\\text{DAG Node Construction: For } x = y \\text{ op } z, \\text{ find or create nodes for } y, z; \\; \\text{if } (\\text{op}, y, z) \\text{ exists, label with } x",
      "\\text{Minimum 3AC Instructions: Equals the number of INTERIOR OPERATOR NODES in the optimized DAG}",
      "\\text{Minimum Temporary Variables: Found via topological node evaluation labeling (Sethi-Ullman algorithm)}"
    ],
    "complexity": "DAG Construction: $O(N)$ operations with hash table value numbering",
    "codeSnippet": "-- DAG Construction for Basic Block:\n-- a = b + c\n-- d = b + c    --> Reuses node (b + c), labels with d!\n-- e = a + d    --> Node (+, a, d) == (+, n1, n1)\n-- Total Operator Nodes in DAG = 2 (instead of 3 instructions!)",
