    "id": "c-dl-number-systems",
    "subjectId": "Digital Logic",
    "chapterId": "dl-number-systems",
    "label": "Positional Number Systems, Radix Conversions & Fractions",
    "name": "Number Systems & Conversions",
    "category": "Number Systems & Computer Arithmetic",
    "kind": "definition",
    "summary": "Positional weighted number system of base/radix $r$. Value of number $(d_{n-1} \\dots d_0 . d_{-1} \\dots d_{-m})_r = \\sum_{i=-m}^{n-1} d_i \\cdot r^i$. Conversions: Base-$r \to$ Decimal (polynomial evaluation); Decimal $\to$ Base-$r$ (Successive division by $r$ for integer part reading remainders bottom-up; Successive multiplication by $r$ for fraction reading integer parts top-down); Direct Binary $\\leftrightarrow$ Octal (group 3 bits), Binary $\\leftrightarrow$ Hexadecimal (group 4 bits).",
    "formula": "N_{10} = \\sum_{i=0}^{n-1} d_i \\cdot r^i + \\sum_{j=1}^{m} d_{-j} \\cdot r^{-j}",
    "keyFormulae": [
      "\\text{Range of integer digits in base } r: \\{0, 1, \\dots, r-1\\}",
      "\\text{Decimal to Base } r \\text{ Integer: Successive division by } r \\implies \\text{Read remainders BOTTOM-UP (LSB to MSB)}",
      "\\text{Decimal to Base } r \\text{ Fraction: Successive multiplication by } r \\implies \\text{Read integer parts TOP-DOWN}",
      "\\text{Grouping: Binary } \\leftrightarrow \\text{Octal } (2^3=8 \\implies 3 \\text{ bits}), \\; \\text{Binary } \\leftrightarrow \\text{Hex } (2^4=16 \\implies 4 \\text{ bits})",
      "\\text{Base Equality: If } (N)_a = (N)_b \\text{ and digits in } a > \\text{ digits in } b \\implies a < b"
    ],
    "complexity": "Conversion: $O(\\log_r N)$ arithmetic division steps",
    "codeSnippet": "# Radix Base Conversion in Python\ndef decimal_to_base_r(n_dec, frac_dec, r, precision=6):\n    # Integer part: successive division\n    int_digits = []\n    n = n_dec\n    while n > 0:\n        int_digits.append(str(n % r))\n        n //= r\n    int_str = ''.join(reversed(int_digits)) or '0'\n    # Fraction part: successive multiplication\n    frac_digits = []\n    f = frac_dec\n    for _ in range(precision):\n        f *= r\n        digit = int(f)\n        frac_digits.append(str(digit))\n        f -= digit\n        if f == 0: break\n    return f\"{int_str}.{''.join(frac_digits)}\"",
    "imageUrl": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 460 120\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect width=\"460\" height=\"120\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#0F172A\"/><rect x=\"25\" y=\"20\" width=\"125\" height=\"85\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#1E293B\" stroke=\"#38BDF8\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"87\" y=\"45\" fill=\"#38BDF8\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Binary (Base 2)</text><text x=\"87\" y=\"72\" fill=\"#CBD5E1\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Bits {0, 1}</text><text x=\"87\" y=\"90\" fill=\"#38BDF8\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\">101101_2</text><rect x=\"165\" y=\"20\" width=\"125\" height=\"85\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#1E293B\" stroke=\"#22C55E\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"227\" y=\"45\" fill=\"#22C55E\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Octal (Base 8)</text><text x=\"227\" y=\"72\" fill=\"#CBD5E1\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Group 3 Bits</text><text x=\"227\" y=\"90\" fill=\"#22C55E\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\">55_8</text><rect x=\"305\" y=\"20\" width=\"130\" height=\"85\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#1E293B\" stroke=\"#F59E0B\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"370\" y=\"45\" fill=\"#F59E0B\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Hex (Base 16)</text><text x=\"370\" y=\"72\" fill=\"#CBD5E1\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Group 4 Bits</text><text x=\"370\" y=\"90\" fill=\"#F59E0B\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2D_16</text></svg>",
    "commonTraps": [
      "When grouping bits for fractional binary to hex/octal (e.g. $0.1011_2$), group from LEFT TO RIGHT, padding trailing zeros on the right.",
      "In base $r$, the maximum single digit value is $r-1$ (e.g. digit $7$ is illegal in base 7).",
      "For solving base equations like $(123)_r = (57)_{10}$, set up the quadratic $1 \\cdot r^2 + 2 \\cdot r + 3 = 57$ and ensure $r > \\max(\\text{digits})$."
    ],
