    "id": "c-dl-overflow-detection",
    "subjectId": "Digital Logic",
    "chapterId": "dl-number-systems",
    "label": "Arithmetic Overflow Detection in Signed vs Unsigned Numbers",
    "name": "Arithmetic Overflow Detection",
    "category": "Number Systems & Computer Arithmetic",
    "kind": "technique",
    "summary": "Overflow occurs when the exact mathematical result of an operation falls OUTSIDE the representable range of the $n$-bit register: 1. Signed 2's Complement Overflow: Occurs IF AND ONLY IF adding two operands of the SAME SIGN produces a result with the OPPOSITE SIGN. Hardware Detection: $V = C_{n-1} \\oplus C_n$ (Carry into MSB XOR Carry out of MSB); 2. Unsigned Overflow: Occurs when carry out of MSB $C_n = 1$.",
    "formula": "V = C_{n-1} \\oplus C_n = A_{n-1} B_{n-1} \\overline{S_{n-1}} + \\overline{A_{n-1}} \\, \\overline{B_{n-1}} S_{n-1}",
    "keyFormulae": [
      "\\text{Hardware Overflow Condition: } V = C_{\\text{in}} \\oplus C_{\\text{out}} \\; (\\text{Carry into MSB } \\oplus \\text{ Carry out of MSB})",
      "\\text{Sign Condition 1: } (+) + (+) = (-) \\implies \\text{OVERFLOW (Positive overflow, result wrapped to negative)}",
      "\\text{Sign Condition 2: } (-) + (-) = (+) \\implies \\text{OVERFLOW (Negative overflow, result wrapped to positive)}",
      "\\text{Opposite Signs: } (+) + (-) \\text{ or } (-) + (+) \\text{ CAN NEVER OVERFLOW!}",
      "\\text{Unsigned Overflow: Detected solely by Carry Flag } C = 1"
    ],
    "complexity": "Detection Delay: Single XOR gate delay $O(1)$",
    "codeSnippet": "# 4-bit Signed Overflow Verifier in Python\ndef detect_signed_overflow(a, b, result_sum, c_in_msb, c_out_msb):\n    # Method 1: Hardware Carry XOR\n    v_hardware = c_in_msb ^ c_out_msb\n    # Method 2: Sign rule\n    sign_a = (a >> 3) & 1\n    sign_b = (b >> 3) & 1\n    sign_s = (result_sum >> 3) & 1\n    v_sign = (sign_a == sign_b) and (sign_s != sign_a)\n    assert v_hardware == v_sign\n    return v_hardware",
    "imageUrl": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 460 120\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect width=\"460\" height=\"120\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#0F172A\"/><rect x=\"25\" y=\"20\" width=\"190\" height=\"75\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#1E293B\" stroke=\"#EF4444\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"45\" fill=\"#EF4444\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">V = Cin \u2295 Cout</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"70\" fill=\"#CBD5E1\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Carry into MSB \u2295 Carry out MSB</text><rect x=\"245\" y=\"20\" width=\"190\" height=\"75\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#1E293B\" stroke=\"#22C55E\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"340\" y=\"45\" fill=\"#22C55E\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Opposite Signs: SAFE</text><text x=\"340\" y=\"70\" fill=\"#22C55E\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">(+) + (-) NEVER causes overflow!</text></svg>",
    "commonTraps": [
      "Adding a positive number and a negative number can NEVER cause overflow.",
      "In unsigned addition, overflow is indicated by $C_{\\text{out}} = 1$; In signed 2's complement, overflow is $C_{\\text{in}} \\oplus C_{\\text{out}} = 1$."
    ],
