    "id": "c-dl-booth-algorithm",
    "subjectId": "Digital Logic",
    "chapterId": "dl-number-systems",
    "label": "Booth's Multiplication Algorithm & Recoding Rules",
    "name": "Booth's Multiplication",
    "category": "Number Systems & Computer Arithmetic",
    "kind": "algorithm",
    "summary": "Multiplication algorithm for signed 2's complement numbers that treats contiguous blocks of 1s efficiently. Replaces string of $k$ consecutive 1s ($2^m + 2^{m-1} + \\dots + 2^{m-k+1}$) with ONE addition at the beginning and ONE subtraction at the end ($2^{m+1} - 2^{m-k+1}$). Recoding table inspects bit pair $(Q_i, Q_{i-1})$: $00 \\to 0$ (Shift), $01 \\to +M$ (Add), $10 \\to -M$ (Subtract), $11 \\to 0$ (Shift). Always followed by Arithmetic Right Shift (ARS).",
    "formula": "(Q_i, Q_{i-1}): \\; 00 \\to 0, \\; 01 \\to +M, \\; 10 \\to -M, \\; 11 \\to 0 \\quad (\\text{Followed by ARS})",
    "keyFormulae": [
      "\\text{Worst Case for Booth: Alternating bits } 01010101_2 \\text{ or } 10101010_2 \\implies n \\text{ additions/subtractions}",
      "\\text{Best Case for Booth: All 0s } (00000000_2) \\text{ or All 1s } (11111111_2) \\implies 0 \\text{ additions/subtractions (Only shifts!)}",
      "\\text{Bit-Pair Modified Booth (Radix-4): Examines 3 bits } (Q_{2i+1}, Q_{2i}, Q_{2i-1}) \\implies \\text{Halves iterations to } n/2",
      "\\text{Arithmetic Right Shift (ARS): Preserves sign bit by replicating MSB into vacant position}"
    ],
    "complexity": "Iterations: Exactly $n$ clock cycles for $n$-bit multiplier ($n/2$ cycles for Radix-4 Booth)",
    "codeSnippet": "# Booth's Multiplier Bit Recoding in Python\ndef booth_recode(multiplier_str):\n    # Append imaginary Q_{-1} = 0\n    extended = multiplier_str + '0'\n    operations = []\n    for i in range(len(multiplier_str) - 1, -1, -1):\n        pair = extended[i:i+2]\n        if pair == '00' or pair == '11': operations.append('SHIFT')\n        elif pair == '01': operations.append('ADD M + SHIFT')\n        elif pair == '10': operations.append('SUB M + SHIFT')\n    return operations",
    "imageUrl": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 460 120\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect width=\"460\" height=\"120\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#0F172A\"/><rect x=\"25\" y=\"20\" width=\"190\" height=\"75\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#1E293B\" stroke=\"#22C55E\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"45\" fill=\"#22C55E\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Best Case: 11111111</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"70\" fill=\"#CBD5E1\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0 Additions/Subtractions</text><rect x=\"245\" y=\"20\" width=\"190\" height=\"75\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#1E293B\" stroke=\"#EF4444\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"340\" y=\"45\" fill=\"#EF4444\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Worst Case: 01010101</text><text x=\"340\" y=\"70\" fill=\"#CBD5E1\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">n Add/Sub Operations</text></svg>",
    "commonTraps": [
      "The initial value of the extra bit $Q_{-1}$ is ALWAYS $0$.",
      "Arithmetic Right Shift MUST preserve the sign bit (replicating the MSB), NOT shift in a zero.",
      "Worst-case multiplier for standard Booth has alternating 0s and 1s ($01010101_2$)."
    ],
