    "id": "c-dl-ieee-754",
    "subjectId": "Digital Logic",
    "chapterId": "dl-number-systems",
    "label": "IEEE 754 Floating-Point Standard (Single & Double Precision)",
    "name": "IEEE 754 Floating Point",
    "category": "Number Systems & Computer Arithmetic",
    "kind": "definition",
    "summary": "Universal standard for binary floating-point representation: 1. Single Precision (32-bit: 1 sign bit $S$, 8 exponent bits $E$, 23 mantissa/fraction bits $M$; Bias $= 127 = 2^{8-1}-1$); 2. Double Precision (64-bit: 1 sign bit $S$, 11 exponent bits $E$, 52 fraction bits $M$; Bias $= 1023 = 2^{11-1}-1$). Normalized Value: $V = (-1)^S \\times 1.M \\times 2^{E - \\text{Bias}}$ (Hidden 1 bit before binary point).",
    "formula": "V = (-1)^S \\times (1.M)_2 \\times 2^{E - \\text{Bias}} \\quad (\\text{Single: Bias} = 127, \\; \\text{Double: Bias} = 1023)",
    "keyFormulae": [
      "\\text{Single Precision: } S (1 \\text{ bit}), \\; E (8 \\text{ bits: } [1, 254]), \\; M (23 \\text{ bits}) \\implies \\text{Bias} = 127",
      "\\text{Double Precision: } S (1 \\text{ bit}), \\; E (11 \\text{ bits: } [1, 2046]), \\; M (52 \\text{ bits}) \\implies \\text{Bias} = 1023",
      "\\text{Decimal to IEEE 754: Convert number to scientific binary } 1.b_1 b_2 \\dots \\times 2^p; \\; E = p + 127; \\; M = b_1 b_2 \\dots 00",
      "\\text{Example: } -0.75_{10} = -0.11_2 = -1.1_2 \\times 2^{-1} \\implies S=1, E=-1+127=126=01111110_2, M=100..0"
    ],
    "complexity": "Precision: Single has ~7 decimal digits of precision; Double has ~16 decimal digits",
    "codeSnippet": "# IEEE-754 Single Precision Encoder in Python\nimport struct\ndef float_to_ieee754_hex(val):\n    # Pack as 32-bit float big-endian\n    packed = struct.pack('>f', val)\n    hex_str = ''.join(f'{b:02X}' for b in packed)\n    bits = ''.join(f'{b:08b}' for b in packed)\n    s, e, m = bits[0], bits[1:9], bits[9:]\n    return hex_str, f\"S={s}, E={e} ({int(e, 2)} - 127), M={m[:6]}...\"",
    "imageUrl": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 460 120\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect width=\"460\" height=\"120\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#0F172A\"/><rect x=\"25\" y=\"35\" width=\"40\" height=\"45\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#1E293B\" stroke=\"#EF4444\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"45\" y=\"55\" fill=\"#EF4444\" font-size=\"10\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">S</text><text x=\"45\" y=\"70\" fill=\"#CBD5E1\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\">1 bit</text><rect x=\"70\" y=\"35\" width=\"130\" height=\"45\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#1E293B\" stroke=\"#38BDF8\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"135\" y=\"55\" fill=\"#38BDF8\" font-size=\"10\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Exponent E (8 bits)</text><text x=\"135\" y=\"70\" fill=\"#CBD5E1\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Bias = 127</text><rect x=\"205\" y=\"35\" width=\"230\" height=\"45\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#1E293B\" stroke=\"#22C55E\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"320\" y=\"55\" fill=\"#22C55E\" font-size=\"10\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Mantissa / Fraction M (23 bits)</text><text x=\"320\" y=\"70\" fill=\"#CBD5E1\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Implicit 1.M (Hidden Bit)</text></svg>",
    "commonTraps": [
      "Do NOT explicitly store the leading '1' in the 23-bit mantissa field (it is an IMPLICIT/HIDDEN bit $1.M$).",
      "Bias is $127$ (NOT 128) for 32-bit single precision, and $1023$ for 64-bit double precision.",
      "The exponent range for normalized numbers is $1 \\le E \\le 254$ ($E=0$ and $E=255$ are reserved for special values!)."
    ],
