    "id": "c-dl-de-morgan",
    "subjectId": "Digital Logic",
    "chapterId": "dl-boolean-algebra",
    "label": "De Morgan's Laws, Dual Functions & Self-Dual Functions Count",
    "name": "De Morgan's Laws & Duals",
    "category": "Boolean Algebra, Logic Gates & Function Minimization",
    "kind": "theorem",
    "summary": "Fundamental complementation laws: 1. $\\overline{A + B} = \\overline{A} \\cdot \\overline{B}$ and $\\overline{A \\cdot B} = \\overline{A} + \\overline{B}$. Dual Function $f^D(x_1, \\dots, x_n)$: Swap $+$ and $\\cdot$, swap $0$ and $1$ ($f^D = \\overline{f(\\overline{x_1}, \\dots, \\overline{x_n})}$). Self-Dual Function: $f = f^D$. Number of self-dual boolean functions of $n$ variables is $2^{2^{n-1}}$. Neutral function: Number of minterms equals maxterms ($2^{n-1}$ minterms).",
    "formula": "\\overline{A_1 + A_2 + \\dots + A_n} = \\overline{A_1} \\cdot \\overline{A_2} \\dots \\overline{A_n}, \\quad \\text{Self-Dual Functions Count} = 2^{2^{n-1}}",
    "keyFormulae": [
      "\\text{De Morgan 1: } \\overline{A + B} = \\overline{A} \\cdot \\overline{B} \\; (\\text{NOR } \\equiv \\text{ Bubbled AND})",
      "\\text{De Morgan 2: } \\overline{A \\cdot B} = \\overline{A} + \\overline{B} \\; (\\text{NAND } \\equiv \\text{ Bubbled OR})",
      "\\text{Dual vs Complement: } f^D \\text{ swaps operators; } f' \\text{ inverts truth table outputs}",
      "\\text{Total Boolean Functions of } n \\text{ variables: } 2^{2^n}",
      "\\text{Self-Dual Functions of } n \\text{ variables: } 2^{2^{n-1}} \\quad (n=1 \\implies 2, \\; n=2 \\implies 4, \\; n=3 \\implies 16, \\; n=4 \\implies 256)"
    ],
    "complexity": "Self-Dual Verification: $f(x) + f(x') = 1$ and $f(x) \\cdot f(x') = 0$",
    "codeSnippet": "-- Self-Dual Function Examples for n=3 (2^(2^2) = 16 functions):\n-- 1. Majority Function: f(A, B, C) = AB + BC + CA (Self-Dual!)\n-- 2. Single Variable: f(A, B, C) = A (Self-Dual!)\n-- 3. Odd Parity: f(A, B, C) = A \u2295 B \u2295 C (Self-Dual!)\n-- Check: f^D(AB + BC + CA) = (A+B)(B+C)(C+A) = AB + BC + CA = f",
    "imageUrl": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 460 120\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect width=\"460\" height=\"120\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#0F172A\"/><rect x=\"25\" y=\"20\" width=\"190\" height=\"75\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#1E293B\" stroke=\"#38BDF8\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"45\" fill=\"#38BDF8\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">De Morgan</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"70\" fill=\"#CBD5E1\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">(A + B)' = A' \u00b7 B' | (AB)' = A' + B'</text><rect x=\"245\" y=\"20\" width=\"190\" height=\"75\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#1E293B\" stroke=\"#22C55E\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"340\" y=\"45\" fill=\"#22C55E\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Self-Dual Count</text><text x=\"340\" y=\"70\" fill=\"#22C55E\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2^(2^(n-1)) Functions</text></svg>",
    "commonTraps": [
      "In finding the DUAL ($f^D$), do NOT complement the variable literals (only swap $+$ and $\\cdot$, and swap $0$ and $1$).",
      "For a function to be self-dual, it must be NEUTRAL (contain exactly $2^{n-1}$ minterms) and contain NO mutually complementary minterm pairs $(m_i, m_{2^n-1-i})$ simultaneously."
    ],
    "pyqMapping": [
      "GATE CSE 2015 Set 1 Q22",
      "GATE CSE 2018 Q21",
      "GATE CSE 2022 Q20"
    ],
    "mindmap": {
      "core": "De Morgan & Duals",
      "branches": [
        "De Morgan's Laws (Bubbled Gates)",
        "Dual Function f^D vs Complement f'",
        "Self-Dual Condition f = f^D",
        "Self-Dual Count Formula 2^(2^(n-1))"
      ]
    },
