    "kind": "algorithm",
    "summary": "NAND and NOR gates are UNIVERSAL gates because any Boolean function can be implemented using NAND gates alone or NOR gates alone. Functionally Complete Sets: $\\{\\text{NAND}\\}$, $\\{\\text{NOR}\\}$, $\\{\\text{AND}, \\text{NOT}\\}$, $\\{\\text{OR}, \\text{NOT}\\}$, $\\{\\text{MUX}\\}$, $\\{\\text{XOR}, \\text{AND}\\}$. Minimum NAND and NOR gate counts to implement standard 2-input logic gates: NOT (1/1), AND (2/3), OR (3/2), NOR (4/1), NAND (1/4), XOR (4/5), XNOR (5/4).",
    "formula": "\\text{Minimum NAND Counts: NOT}(1), \\text{AND}(2), \\text{OR}(3), \\text{XOR}(4), \\text{XNOR}(5)",
