    "id": "c-dl-xor-xnor-properties",
    "subjectId": "Digital Logic",
    "chapterId": "dl-boolean-algebra",
    "label": "XOR and XNOR Gates Properties, Controlled Inverter & Parity",
    "name": "XOR / XNOR Properties & Parity",
    "category": "Boolean Algebra, Logic Gates & Function Minimization",
    "kind": "technique",
    "summary": "Properties of XOR ($\\oplus$) and XNOR ($\\odot$): 1. XOR (Modulo-2 Addition): $A \\oplus B = A'B + AB'$; $A \\oplus 0 = A$ (Buffer), $A \\oplus 1 = A'$ (Controlled Inverter), $A \\oplus A = 0$, $A \\oplus A' = 1$; 2. Associative & Commutative; 3. Odd Function: Multi-input XOR outputs 1 IF AND ONLY IF an ODD number of inputs are 1 (Used in Parity Generators); 4. For $n$ variables, $(x_1 \\oplus x_2 \\dots \\oplus x_n)' = x_1 \\oplus x_2 \\dots \\oplus x_n'$ (If $n$ is even, XOR negated $\\equiv$ XNOR; if $n$ is odd, XOR $\\equiv$ XNOR!).",
    "formula": "A \\oplus B = A\\overline{B} + \\overline{A}B, \\quad A \\oplus 0 = A, \\quad A \\oplus 1 = \\overline{A}, \\quad A \\oplus A = 0, \\quad A \\oplus \\overline{A} = 1",
    "keyFormulae": [
      "\\text{Controlled Inverter: If Control } C=0 \\implies \\text{Output } = A; \\; \\text{If Control } C=1 \\implies \\text{Output } = A'",
      "\\text{Odd Number of Variables } n: x_1 \\odot x_2 \\dots \\odot x_n = x_1 \\oplus x_2 \\dots \\oplus x_n",
      "\\text{Even Number of Variables } n: x_1 \\odot x_2 \\dots \\odot x_n = \\overline{x_1 \\oplus x_2 \\dots \\oplus x_n}",
      "\\text{Parity Generator: Odd Parity Bit } P = A \\oplus B \\oplus C \\oplus \\dots; \\; \\text{Even Parity Bit } P = (A \\oplus B \\oplus \\dots)'"
    ],
    "complexity": "Parity Checking: $O(\\log n)$ tree of 2-input XOR gates",
    "codeSnippet": "-- XOR Controlled Inverter in Adder/Subtractor:\n-- Full Adder with XOR on B input with control bit M (Mode):\n-- If M = 0: B \u2295 0 = B and Cin = 0  --> Performs A + B (Addition)\n-- If M = 1: B \u2295 1 = B' and Cin = 1 --> Performs A + B' + 1 = A - B (Subtraction!)",
    "imageUrl": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 460 120\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect width=\"460\" height=\"120\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#0F172A\"/><rect x=\"25\" y=\"20\" width=\"190\" height=\"75\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#1E293B\" stroke=\"#38BDF8\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"45\" fill=\"#38BDF8\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Controlled Inverter</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"70\" fill=\"#CBD5E1\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">A \u2295 0 = A | A \u2295 1 = A'</text><rect x=\"245\" y=\"20\" width=\"190\" height=\"75\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#1E293B\" stroke=\"#22C55E\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"340\" y=\"45\" fill=\"#22C55E\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Odd Function (Parity)</text><text x=\"340\" y=\"70\" fill=\"#22C55E\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Outputs 1 if Odd Number of 1s</text></svg>",
    "commonTraps": [
      "For 3 variables: $A \\odot B \\odot C = A \\oplus B \\oplus C$ (XNOR and XOR are IDENTICAL for any odd number of variables!).",
      "For 2 variables: $A \\odot B = (A \\oplus B)'$ (XNOR is the negation of XOR for any even number of variables)."
    ],
