    "id": "c-dl-encoders-priority",
    "subjectId": "Digital Logic",
    "chapterId": "dl-combinational-circuits",
    "label": "Binary Encoders, Priority Encoders & Valid Bit",
    "name": "Encoders & Priority Encoders",
    "category": "Combinational Circuit Building Blocks",
    "kind": "definition",
    "summary": "Inverse operation of decoder: converts 1-hot input into binary code. Standard $2^n$-to-$n$ Encoder: Assumes exactly one input is active. Priority Encoder: Handles multiple simultaneous active inputs by establishing strict priority order (highest-index active input wins). Valid Output Bit $V$: Indicates whether AT LEAST ONE input is active ($V = D_0 + D_1 + \\dots + D_{2^n-1}$).",
    "formula": "\\text{4-to-2 Priority Encoder: } A_1 = D_3 + D_2, \\quad A_0 = D_3 + D_2' D_1, \\quad V = D_3 + D_2 + D_1 + D_0",
    "keyFormulae": [
      "\\text{Priority Order: } D_3 > D_2 > D_1 > D_0 \\; (D_3 \\text{ has highest priority})",
      "\\text{Output Equations: } A_1 = D_3 + D_2, \\quad A_0 = D_3 + \\overline{D_2} D_1",
      "\\text{Valid Bit } V: V=1 \\text{ if any } D_i=1; \\; V=0 \\text{ if all } D_i=0 \\; (\\text{Distinguishes valid 00 from idle state})",
      "\\text{Octal-to-Binary Priority Encoder (8-to-3): Produces 3-bit binary output for highest active line}"
    ],
    "complexity": "Hardware Realization: 2-level gate logic using don't-care conditions",
    "codeSnippet": "# 4-to-2 Priority Encoder Logic in Python\ndef priority_encoder_4to2(d3, d2, d1, d0):\n    v = d3 | d2 | d1 | d0\n    if not v: return None, None, 0 # Invalid / Idle\n    a1 = d3 | d2\n    a0 = d3 | ((not d2) & d1)\n    return a1, a0, 1 # A1, A0, Valid bit",
    "imageUrl": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 460 120\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect width=\"460\" height=\"120\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#0F172A\"/><rect x=\"25\" y=\"20\" width=\"190\" height=\"75\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#1E293B\" stroke=\"#38BDF8\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"45\" fill=\"#38BDF8\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Priority Selection</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"70\" fill=\"#CBD5E1\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Highest active line wins (D3 &gt; D2 &gt; D1)</text><rect x=\"245\" y=\"20\" width=\"190\" height=\"75\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#1E293B\" stroke=\"#22C55E\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"340\" y=\"45\" fill=\"#22C55E\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Valid Bit (V)</text><text x=\"340\" y=\"70\" fill=\"#22C55E\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">V = D3 + D2 + D1 + D0</text></svg>",
    "commonTraps": [
      "Without the Valid bit ($V$), the encoder cannot distinguish between $D_0=1$ active (output `00`) and NO inputs active (all zero, output `00`).",
      "In priority encoders, don't-care conditions ($X$) represent lower-priority inputs once a higher-priority input is active."
    ],
