    "name": "Code Converters & BCD",
    "category": "Combinational Circuit Building Blocks",
    "kind": "algorithm",
    "summary": "Circuit transformations between binary representations: 1. Binary to Gray Code: $G_n = B_n, G_i = B_{i+1} \\oplus B_i$ (Single bit changes between adjacent numbers, unit-distance code); 2. Gray Code to Binary: $B_n = G_n, B_i = B_{i+1} \\oplus G_i$; 3. BCD (Binary Coded Decimal: 8421): Digits $0-9$ encoded in 4 bits; 4. BCD Adder: When sum $> 9$ ($1001_2$) or carry $K=1$, ADD CORRECTION $+6$ ($0110_2$). Correction Condition: $C = K + S_3 S_2 + S_3 S_1$.",
    "formula": "G_i = B_{i+1} \\oplus B_i \\quad | \\quad B_i = B_{i+1} \\oplus G_i \\quad | \\quad \\text{BCD Correction Condition: } C = K + S_3 S_2 + S_3 S_1",
    "keyFormulae": [
      "\\text{Binary to Gray: } G_3 = B_3, \\; G_2 = B_3 \\oplus B_2, \\; G_1 = B_2 \\oplus B_1, \\; G_0 = B_1 \\oplus B_0",
      "\\text{Gray to Binary: } B_3 = G_3, \\; B_2 = B_3 \\oplus G_2, \\; B_1 = B_2 \\oplus G_1, \\; B_0 = B_1 \\oplus G_0",
      "\\text{BCD Valid Range: } [0, 9] \\; (0000_2 \\dots 1001_2); \\; \\text{Invalid BCD: } [10, 15] \\; (1010_2 \\dots 1111_2)",
      "\\text{BCD Adder Circuit: 4-bit Binary Adder } + \\text{ Correction Logic } (C = K + S_3 S_2 + S_3 S_1) + \\text{ Second 4-bit Adder (adds } 0110_2)"
    ],
    "complexity": "Conversion: $n-1$ XOR gates for $n$-bit Binary/Gray conversion",
    "codeSnippet": "# Binary <-> Gray Code in Python\ndef binary_to_gray(b_int):\n    return b_int ^ (b_int >> 1)\n\ndef gray_to_binary(g_int):\n    b = 0\n    while g_int > 0:\n        b ^= g_int\n        g_int >>= 1\n    return b",
    "imageUrl": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 460 120\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect width=\"460\" height=\"120\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#0F172A\"/><rect x=\"25\" y=\"20\" width=\"190\" height=\"75\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#1E293B\" stroke=\"#38BDF8\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"45\" fill=\"#38BDF8\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Binary \u2194 Gray</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"70\" fill=\"#CBD5E1\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Gi = B(i+1) \u2295 Bi | Bi = B(i+1) \u2295 Gi</text><rect x=\"245\" y=\"20\" width=\"190\" height=\"75\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#1E293B\" stroke=\"#22C55E\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"340\" y=\"45\" fill=\"#22C55E\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">BCD Correction (+6)</text><text x=\"340\" y=\"70\" fill=\"#22C55E\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">C = K + S3\u00b7S2 + S3\u00b7S1</text></svg>",
    "commonTraps": [
      "In BCD addition, correction $+6$ ($0110_2$) is required IF sum $> 9$ OR carry out $K=1$.",
      "Binary to Gray conversion uses ADJACENT BINARY BITS ($B_{i+1} \\oplus B_i$); Gray to Binary conversion cascades the PREVIOUSLY COMPUTED BINARY BIT ($B_{i+1} \\oplus G_i$)."
    ],
