    "category": "Combinational Circuit Building Blocks",
    "kind": "definition",
    "summary": "Configurable semiconductor devices implementing combinational logic: 1. PROM (Programmable Read-Only Memory): Fixed AND array (full decoder generating all $2^n$ minterms), Programmable OR array; 2. PAL (Programmable Array Logic): Programmable AND array, Fixed OR array (faster, cheaper, no shared product terms); 3. PLA (Programmable Logic Array): Programmable AND array, Programmable OR array (most flexible, allows sharing product terms across multiple outputs).",
    "formula": "\\text{PROM: Fixed AND / Prog OR} \\quad | \\quad \\text{PAL: Prog AND / Fixed OR} \\quad | \\quad \\text{PLA: Prog AND / Prog OR}",
    "keyFormulae": [
      "\\text{PROM: Generates ALL } 2^n \\text{ minterms via fixed decoder; Cannot be optimized with K-maps}",
      "\\text{PAL: Fastest programmable logic (fixed OR array reduces propagation delay)}",
      "\\text{PLA: Best for multiple-output functions sharing common product terms}",
      "\\text{FPGA (Field Programmable Gate Array): Configurable Logic Blocks (CLBs) with LUTs and Flip-Flops}"
    ],
    "complexity": "Flexibility: $\\text{PROM} < \\text{PAL} < \\text{PLA}$; Speed: $\\text{PAL} > \\text{PLA} > \\text{PROM}$",
