    "label": "SR and D Latches: NOR/NAND Implementations & Metastability",
    "name": "Latches & Metastability",
    "category": "Sequential Circuits & Latches/Flip-Flops",
    "kind": "definition",
    "summary": "Level-sensitive bistable memory elements: 1. NOR-based SR Latch: Cross-coupled NOR gates. Active-High ($S=1, R=0 \\implies Q=1; S=0, R=1 \\implies Q=0; S=0, R=0 \\implies \\text{Hold}$; $S=1, R=1$ is FORBIDDEN / Invalid); 2. NAND-based SR Latch: Cross-coupled NAND gates. Active-Low ($S'=0, R'=0$ is FORBIDDEN); 3. Gated D Latch (Transparent Latch): Eliminates invalid state by connecting $R = S' = D'$ ($Q = D$ when $EN=1$; Holds state when $EN=0$).",
    "formula": "\\text{NOR SR Latch: } Q_{n+1} = S + R' Q_n \\quad (\\text{Constraint: } SR = 0)",
    "keyFormulae": [
      "\\text{NOR SR Latch (Active-High): } S=1, R=1 \\implies Q=0, Q'=0 \\; (\\text{Forbidden! When inputs drop to 00 } \\implies \\text{Metastable race})",
      "\\text{NAND S'R' Latch (Active-Low): } S'=0, R'=0 \\implies Q=1, Q'=1 \\; (\\text{Forbidden})",
      "\\text{Gated D Latch: } Q_{\\text{next}} = D \\cdot EN + Q \\cdot \\overline{EN}",
      "\\text{Metastability: Undefined intermediate voltage state when timing constraints are violated}"
    ],
    "complexity": "Storage: 1-bit memory using 2 cross-coupled inverting gates",
    "codeSnippet": "-- SR Latch Truth Tables:\n-- NOR SR Latch (Active-High):       NAND S'R' Latch (Active-Low):\n-- S  R  Q(next)  State             S' R' Q(next)  State\n-- 0  0  Q        Hold              0  0  1/1      FORBIDDEN\n-- 0  1  0        Reset             0  1  1        Set\n-- 1  0  1        Set               1  0  0        Reset\n-- 1  1  0/0      FORBIDDEN         1  1  Q        Hold",
    "imageUrl": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 460 120\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect width=\"460\" height=\"120\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#0F172A\"/><rect x=\"25\" y=\"20\" width=\"190\" height=\"75\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#1E293B\" stroke=\"#38BDF8\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"45\" fill=\"#38BDF8\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">NOR SR Latch</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"70\" fill=\"#CBD5E1\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Active-High | Forbidden: S=1, R=1</text><rect x=\"245\" y=\"20\" width=\"190\" height=\"75\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#1E293B\" stroke=\"#22C55E\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"340\" y=\"45\" fill=\"#22C55E\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Gated D Latch</text><text x=\"340\" y=\"70\" fill=\"#22C55E\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Transparent when EN=1 (No forbidden)</text></svg>",
    "commonTraps": [
      "In a NOR-based SR latch, the forbidden state is $S=1, R=1$; In a NAND-based S'R' latch, the forbidden state is $S'=0, R'=0$.",
      "Latches are LEVEL-sensitive (transparent during clock pulse); Flip-Flops are EDGE-triggered."
    ],
